7Nc4yqEikAyvv6q7+1997NOhowi1CrcrL\nLScO\n=o30G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-24T22:11:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1560381?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tjementum","id":1560381,"login":"tjementum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjAzODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commit/2814ab963b5f64454b4655a086787c4d01120b2c","node_id":"C_kwDOJY2PLtoAKDI4MTRhYjk2M2I1ZjY0NDU0YjQ2NTVhMDg2Nzg3YzRkMDExMjBiMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commit/ec1859a4135db4c35801983c7f65923d4c9cb7f8","sha":"ec1859a4135db4c35801983c7f65923d4c9cb7f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/ec1859a4135db4c35801983c7f65923d4c9cb7f8"}],"sha":"2814ab963b5f64454b4655a086787c4d01120b2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/2814ab963b5f64454b4655a086787c4d01120b2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1560381?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tjementum","id":1560381,"login":"tjementum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjAzODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/ec1859a4135db4c35801983c7f65923d4c9cb7f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T15:41:33Z","email":"tje@platformplatform.net","name":"Thomas Jespersen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T15:41:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Replace per-test database reseeding with a snapshot restore in backend tests (#910)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nBackend endpoint tests recreated the schema with `EnsureCreated()` and\nreran the full `DatabaseSeeder` on a fresh in-memory SQLite connection\nfor every test, so the cost of seeding was paid again on every test and\ngrew with every fixture added to the seeder. This change seeds the\nschema and fixtures once into a template database and fills each test''s\nconnection with a binary copy through `SqliteConnection.BackupDatabase`.\nThe restore cost is effectively constant in the number of fixtures, so\nseeding no longer scales with the size of the seed data.\n\n- The `account` endpoint, back-office, and external-authentication base\ntests now restore from a shared seeded template\n(`SeededDatabaseTemplate`) instead of calling `EnsureCreated()` and\nreseeding per test. The template is seeded once through the real\ndependency injection graph so Entity Framework interceptors behave as in\nproduction, and a lock serializes the binary copies that feed each test.\n- The `main` test infrastructure is brought to parity with `account`: a\nsingle host shared per test class (`MainWebApplicationFactory`, with\nper-test state carried through an `AsyncLocal` `MainTestContext`) plus\nthe same snapshot seeding, replacing the per-test host rebuild. The\n`main` system has no endpoint tests yet, so this establishes the shared\npattern for the first one.\n- The size of the gain tracks the size of the fixtures. With today''s\nsmall `account` fixtures the full backend suite drops from about 22.0 to\nabout 20.9 seconds averaged over five runs. A controlled measurement\nthat added 1,000 seed rows raised the per-test reseed approach to about\n49 seconds while the snapshot held at about 20, so the gap grows from a\nfew percent to well over half as fixtures expand.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","tree":{"sha":"c5b871a8e9d3a578ca5a3ab8662a1dbee8d48aaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/git/trees/c5b871a8e9d3a578ca5a3ab8662a1dbee8d48aaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/git/commits/ec1859a4135db4c35801983c7f65923d4c9cb7f8","verification":{"payload":"tree c5b871a8e9d3a578ca5a3ab8662a1dbee8d48aaa\nparent 66d1fc52a8295986d1d38b476dc6803b683d08fb\nparent befe4db989ec2819914f876c37e3246980e9ff0b\nauthor Thomas Jespersen <tje@platformplatform.net> 1782229293 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782229293 +0200\n\nReplace per-test database reseeding with a snapshot restore in backend tests (#910)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nBackend endpoint tests recreated the schema with `EnsureCreated()` and\nreran the full `DatabaseSeeder` on a fresh in-memory SQLite connection\nfor every test, so the cost of seeding was paid again on every test and\ngrew with every fixture added to the seeder. This change seeds the\nschema and fixtures once into a template database and fills each test''s\nconnection with a binary copy through `SqliteConnection.BackupDatabase`.\nThe restore cost is effectively constant in the number of fixtures, so\nseeding no longer scales with the size of the seed data.\n\n- The `account` endpoint, back-office, and external-authentication base\ntests now restore from a shared seeded template\n(`SeededDatabaseTemplate`) instead of calling `EnsureCreated()` and\nreseeding per test. The template is seeded once through the real\ndependency injection graph so Entity Framework interceptors behave as in\nproduction, and a lock serializes the binary copies that feed each test.\n- The `main` test infrastructure is brought to parity with `account`: a\nsingle host shared per test class (`MainWebApplicationFactory`, with\nper-test state carried through an `AsyncLocal` `MainTestContext`) plus\nthe same snapshot seeding, replacing the per-test host rebuild. The\n`main` system has no endpoint tests yet, so this establishes the shared\npattern for the first one.\n- The size of the gain tracks the size of the fixtures. With today''s\nsmall `account` fixtures the full backend suite drops from about 22.0 to\nabout 20.9 seconds averaged over five runs. A controlled measurement\nthat added 1,000 seed rows raised the per-test reseed approach to about\n49 seconds while the snapshot held at about 20, so the gap grows from a\nfew percent to well over half as fixtures expand.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOqktCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdwcQAIBs63fvwSMYjo1f8plAbLT1\n2nogP9ZpaVGeH8c3IUGoAjjytfJe3pYFK4R4IOBqzUdpaOKvF+tYz/ZAbvmr+5cn\nb7wSBdD3g3jUNmE26/MhxWdhX644wEk27Pmw/0Q3o8LYF5+KZbtA0q9Xay2dtKD1\nSnPs7Oe64iyhYg86NwLSqqWqWesjXtu4qMc