a":"205b6711a9053c57507ab813e84a14b523a4fb9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/205b6711a9053c57507ab813e84a14b523a4fb9a"}],"sha":"131f2b7b4eee2adad72556b934fea770e9a33c75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/131f2b7b4eee2adad72556b934fea770e9a33c75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1560381?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tjementum","id":1560381,"login":"tjementum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjAzODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/205b6711a9053c57507ab813e84a14b523a4fb9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T17:30:20Z","email":"tje@platformplatform.net","name":"Thomas Jespersen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T17:30:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop format command from converting local clones to shallow clones (#900)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nThe developer CLI''s `format` command silently converted full local\nclones into shallow clones. `GitHelper.GetChangedCsFilesInDirectory` ran\n`git fetch origin main --depth=1` before computing the changed-`.cs`\ndiff, with the stated goal of supporting shallow CI checkouts. Against a\nfull clone, that fetch creates `.git/shallow` containing the tip of\n`origin/main` — truncating `main`''s reachable history to a single commit\non the developer''s machine. The change is silent and only becomes\nvisible later when a Git GUI renders `main` as disconnected from its own\nhistory. Recovery requires `git fetch --unshallow`, which is not\ndiscoverable.\n\nAuditing the workflows that actually call `format` (`code-style.yml`,\n`account.yml`, `main.yml`), every one of them already checks out with\n`fetch-depth: 0`. The shallow workaround is dead code in every\nenvironment in which it runs — it cannot help CI (CI is already full)\nand only harms local developers. If a future workflow ever needs to run\n`format` against a shallow checkout, the right place to fix that is at\nthe checkout step, not in `GitHelper`.\n\nThe depth-1 fetch is removed outright and the inline comment rewritten\nto make the new contract explicit: the method relies on the caller''s\nenvironment to keep `origin/main` reasonably current.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","tree":{"sha":"89acc70ffaa7022bf4e923d11cc841851c1861cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/git/trees/89acc70ffaa7022bf4e923d11cc841851c1861cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/git/commits/205b6711a9053c57507ab813e84a14b523a4fb9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 89acc70ffaa7022bf4e923d11cc841851c1861cc\nparent 74e5c114022a11b24efc3ab02ba7fe2f1630d52e\nparent 913a70f1c8ab5b2c82e5f54a7f0f63f361aaaaf6\nauthor Thomas Jespersen <tje@platformplatform.net> 1779384620 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779384620 +0200\n\nStop format command from converting local clones to shallow clones (#900)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nThe developer CLI''s `format` command silently converted full local\nclones into shallow clones. `GitHelper.GetChangedCsFilesInDirectory` ran\n`git fetch origin main --depth=1` before computing the changed-`.cs`\ndiff, with the stated goal of supporting shallow CI checkouts. Against a\nfull clone, that fetch creates `.git/shallow` containing the tip of\n`origin/main` — truncating `main`''s reachable history to a single commit\non the developer''s machine. The change is silent and only becomes\nvisible later when a Git GUI renders `main` as disconnected from its own\nhistory. Recovery requires `git fetch --unshallow`, which is not\ndiscoverable.\n\nAuditing the workflows that actually call `format` (`code-style.yml`,\n`account.yml`, `main.yml`), every one of them already checks out with\n`fetch-depth: 0`. The shallow workaround is dead code in every\nenvironment in which it runs — it cannot help CI (CI is already full)\nand only harms local developers. If a future workflow ever needs to run\n`format` against a shallow checkout, the right place to fix that is at\nthe checkout step, not in `GitHelper`.\n\nThe depth-1 fetch is removed outright and the inline comment rewritten\nto make the new contract explicit: the method relies on the caller''s\nenvironment to keep `origin/main` reasonably current.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqD0EsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdMgQAKe4knVK7PmRNTiEl8+a7wO0\n38SvyBMyNyO0JgWzje4k4Dho5KLsSyR9XWJ0QJcczCQ7px6pJsrpmf1yhiwZ6zqW\nIqkidV6sUCS/TDvWGmbjOoatLqZFf3RJGmlCiBjaWXTDLFgZQCWSVkks+/qC5rDg\nSis6xQJCIBgu6ICGkNmjO+ifyxOTmiNHkqvSPOZZLZJdE8c7Lw3SaQ5Ez71FpXgi\n8GernvDByEacDpVwfJizcc5kctFuQdWnLqAWdZx4K+03V448vp5Ret+w9PNeGCwk\nhzPWW1kVBjbkA0wPTLDtTyiqDvXWC347ph4YqmNydamzhlxz/3ie0HUzMUOhlJUk\nLqeO7yhK8Y/pA98Kc/VI4gwBu2Uvbpy5Ex08vpEn7fLRgA4Imu/9ZCq4V/IIke/K\nlGu8VnaMRljHddlo1SQiAL9lGxV4budA0n5AKWMgo8TztTxX/TzEVpp5I9QMxnRm\ns65uZvbJoQAKPFq2ed3jjL9lS7UOLImZXd5r