2e\nauthor Thomas Jespersen <tje@platformplatform.net> 1779384100 +0200\ncommitter Thomas Jespersen <tje@platformplatform.net> 1779384100 +0200\n\nStop format command from converting local clones to shallow clones\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQTft1bMTMJHM0wcYmtJt8eguw4NgUCag8/JAAKCRCtJt8eguw4\nNhoTAQCosOfWir9NUXJCkEi+wrVgKh3VhZkdvH97cQvPqOqT5AD/fa9x1NzxV/1h\ng62e3KPLDV0fGOV2a314s2VlBmyBwQw=\n=PMLj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-21T17:21:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1560381?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tjementum","id":1560381,"login":"tjementum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjAzODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commit/913a70f1c8ab5b2c82e5f54a7f0f63f361aaaaf6","node_id":"C_kwDOJY2PLtoAKDkxM2E3MGYxYzhhYjViMmM4MmU1ZjU0YTdmMGY2M2YzNjFhYWFhZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commit/74e5c114022a11b24efc3ab02ba7fe2f1630d52e","sha":"74e5c114022a11b24efc3ab02ba7fe2f1630d52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/74e5c114022a11b24efc3ab02ba7fe2f1630d52e"}],"sha":"913a70f1c8ab5b2c82e5f54a7f0f63f361aaaaf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/913a70f1c8ab5b2c82e5f54a7f0f63f361aaaaf6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1560381?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tjementum","id":1560381,"login":"tjementum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjAzODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/commits/74e5c114022a11b24efc3ab02ba7fe2f1630d52e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T22:49:18Z","email":"tje@platformplatform.net","name":"Thomas Jespersen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T22:49:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Centralize branding so a rebrand touches only configuration and assets (#898)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nPlatformPlatform''s brand identity was hardcoded across the codebase —\nthe product name, colors, logos, emails, taglines, social links, and\ndeployment configuration each carried literal values in source files.\nRebranding meant hunting through the backend, the SPA, email templates,\ninfrastructure scripts, and CI workflows.\n\nThis change pulls every brand surface behind two things: a single\nconfiguration file and a fixed set of logo assets. A rebrand becomes a\nclosed, predictable operation:\n\n- Edit `application/platform-settings.jsonc` — product name, primary\ncolor, PWA theme and background colors, email header background,\nper-locale taglines, contact and support emails, social links, internal\nemail domain, the \"Add to Home Screen\" toggle, and the local Docker\nvolume prefix.\n- Replace the logo assets in place at their canonical paths — the\nwordmark and mark in `shared-webapp/ui/images`, the favicon and\napple-touch icons in the `public` folders, the hero images, and the\nemail banner. File names and dimensions are fixed, so the replacements\nare drop-in.\n\nThe `rebrand` skill added here documents the full process step by step.\n\n**Brand configuration**\n\n- Add `application/platform-settings.jsonc` as the single source of\ntruth — embedded into the backend as an embedded resource and injected\ninto the frontend at build time.\n- Wire every brand surface to it: SPA strings, the \"Add to Home Screen\"\nprompt, the delete-account support email, transactional email templates,\nPWA manifests, and HTML and backend API titles (including the Back\nOffice title). The E2E suite reads the product name from the same file,\nso tests stay green after a rebrand.\n- Centralize brand colors through the file — the primary color, the PWA\ntheme and background colors, and the transactional email header\nbackground.\n- Add per-locale taglines split across web and mail channels, and a\n`showAddToHomescreen` flag that gates the iOS install prompt.\n- Source the cluster deployment''s product name from the same file via\n`deploy-cluster.sh`, so deployment branding follows the config with no\nseparate CI variable.\n\n**Brand assets**\n\n- Centralize brand logos and hero images in `shared-webapp/ui/images`\nand remove the duplicated per-app copies. A theme-aware `Logo` component\nresolves the light or dark variant automatically and preserves the\naspect ratio of non-square marks.\n- Make the transactional email header a full-width responsive banner\nthat scales on mobile, and drop the card corner radius on small screens.\n- Add dedicated `platformplatform-*` credit logos, kept separate from\nthe configurable assets so upstream attribution survives a rebrand.\n\n**Developer experience**\n\n- Make the developer CLI alias and its user-facing messages derive from\nconfiguration.\n- Centralize the Docker volume prefix in `platform-settings.jsonc`\n(`development.dockerVolumePrefix`), resolved by a shared helper so the\nAspire AppHost and the CLI `stop` command always agree.\n- Reorganize the local development port allocation so the browser-facing\nhosts take the lowest offsets, with a slot reserved for a future `web`\nhost.\n- Move the `/components` design-system showcase into the back-office so\nit sits behind authentication, and serve email preview artifacts only\nthere. The preview now renders real brand values instead of stale sample\ndata.\n- Fix the account and main staging deploy jobs so they no longer skip\nwhen the database migration job is skipped — a change carrying the\n`Deploy to Staging` label with no migration changes now deploys to\nstaging as expected.\n\n**UI and content fixes**\n\n- Constrain the landing and legal pages to a 1024px content width with\nedge-aligned navigation, restructure the landing page footer, and fix\nlogo sizing in narrow navigation headers and on error pages.\n- Remove the region selector from the signup form and the \"Built with\nPlatformPlatform\" attribution from the login and verification footers.\n- Fix Danish translation errors and adopt the \"compliance\" loanword.\n\nMinor fixes: remove an orphaned `PlatformPlatform.*` coverage filter,\nadd a dark-mode `apple-touch-icon`, replace brand SVGs with PNGs so\nSafari renders them crisply, track `platform-settings.jsonc` as a turbo\nglobal dependency, and use `example.com` in illustrative comments.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","tree":{"sha":"5e05afe6f927e5d47e893c2e6ca2103a6617c9fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/git/trees/5e05afe6f927e5d47e893c2e6ca2103a6617c9fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformplatform/PlatformPlatform/git/commits/74e5c114022a11b24efc3ab02ba7fe2f1630d52e","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e05afe6f927e5d47e893c2e6ca2103a6617c9fe\nparent aff1d63ecab421e83b1d43f4edfdda81bb126fcc\nparent e84038d8282d3d2670804adb4592d18951b5f066\nauthor Thomas Jespersen <tje@platformplatform.net> 1779230958 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779230958 +0200\n\nCentralize branding so a rebrand touches only configuration and assets (#898)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nPlatformPlatform''s brand identity was hardcoded across the codebase —\nthe product name, colors, logos, emails, taglines, social links, and\ndeployment configuration each carried literal values in source files.\nRebranding meant hunting through the backend, the SPA, email templates,\ninfrastructure scripts, and CI workflows.\n\nThis change pulls every brand surface behind two things: a single\nconfiguration file and a fixed set of logo assets. A rebrand becomes a\nclosed, predictable operation:\n\n- Edit `application/platform-settings.jsonc` — product name, primary\ncolor, PWA theme and background colors, email header background,\nper-locale taglines, contact and support emails, social links, internal\nemail domain, the \"Add to Home Screen\" toggle, and the local Docker\nvolume prefix.\n- Replace the logo assets in place at their canonical paths — the\nwordmark and mark in `shared-webapp/ui/images`, the favicon and\napple-touch icons in the `public` folders, the hero images, and the\nemail banner. File names and dimensions are fixed, so the replacements\nare drop-in.\n\nThe `rebrand` skill added here documents the full process step by step.\n\n**Brand configuration**\n\n- Add `application/platform-settings.jsonc` as the single source of\ntruth — embedded into the backend as an embedded resource and injected\ninto the frontend at build time.\n- Wire every brand surface to it: SPA strings, the \"Add to Home Screen\"\nprompt, the delete-account support email, transactional email templates,\nPWA manifests, and HTML and backend API titles (including the Back\nOffice title). The E2E suite reads the product name from the same file,\nso tests stay green after a rebrand.\n- Centralize brand colors through the file — the primary color, the PWA\ntheme and background colors, and the transactional email header\nbackground.\n- Add per-locale taglines split across web and mail channels, and a\n`showAddToHomescreen` flag that gates the iOS install prompt.\n- Source the cluster deployment''s product name from the same file via\n`deploy-cluster.sh`, so deployment branding follows the config with no\nseparate CI variable.\n\n**Brand assets**\n\n- Centralize brand logos and hero images in `shared-webapp/ui/images`\nand remove the duplicated per-app copies. A theme-aware `Logo` component\nresolves the light or dark variant automatically and preserves the\naspect ratio of non-square marks.\n- Make the transactional email header a full-width responsive banner\nthat scales on mobile, and drop the card corner radius on small screens.\n- Add dedicated `platformplatform-*` credit logos, kept separate from\nthe configurable assets so upstream attribution survives a rebrand.\n\n**Developer experience**\n\n- Make the developer CLI alias and its user-facing messages derive from\nconfiguration.\n- Centralize the Docker volume prefix in `platform-settings.jsonc`\n(`development.dockerVolumePrefix`), resolved by a shared helper so the\nAspire AppHost and the CLI `stop` command always agree.\n- Reorganize the local development port allocation so the browser-facing\nhosts take the lowest offsets, with a slot reserved for a future `web`\nhost.\n- Move the `/components` design-system showcase into the back-office so\nit sits behind authentication, and serve email preview artifacts only\nthere. The preview now renders real brand values instead of stale sample\ndata.\n- Fix the account and main staging deploy jobs so they no longer skip\nwhen the database migration job is skipped — a change carrying the\n`Deploy to Staging` label with no migration changes now deploys to\nstaging as expected.\n\n**UI and content fixes**\n\n- Constrain the landing and legal pages to a 1024px content width with\nedge-aligned navigation, restructure the landing page footer, and fix\nlogo sizing in narrow navigation headers and on error pages.\n- Remove the region selector from the signup form and the \"Built with\nPlatformPlatform\" attribution from the login and verification footers.\n- Fix Danish translation errors and adopt the \"compliance\" loanword.\n\nMinor fixes: remove an orphaned `PlatformPlatform.*` coverage filter,\nadd a dark-mode `apple-touch-icon`, replace brand SVGs with PNGs so\nSafari renders them crisply, track `platform-settings.jsonc` as a turbo\nglobal dependency, and use `example.com` in illustrative comments.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDOjuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQP4QABadzKbcbdTgkS04ghlgJxAq\n88mF+em6MYWaLmMEMUCq+DlbEJlkRjjJ+aMdtancvb/a8/0kzM4QyDhm2SrPRbOF\nNh8R+A2dHr8OnMpmCV+yIMCpTXmwnLM4TptYySo5KGIk4JDB+4DP2F4aILTiSakq\nef+UTR7s/8HemYMDthcaDn6bJ3IaM1d5yU8x6Eiqz0sOO40FQxJMWFs9IJXb5z1q\nkgZDppq9LRKD/zciKEQaXj9N+dYrWQ1RAsKdFppC6R+Dxqe0XYWwX7HnM8hpxH4n\ns+emHHxosZwRV0+0wT5Nkr3BD+LKcKoMLyhKFA1tYtb3KFJpllCiRpSBUQYf9MC+\n+9Rd6P0iSF/p5GfSr6R/XtBfJA2u4241jEpUeemSh4RhsAJdXiRnIc4xK2jB1GL4\nsQhKaknZB8yinXkxMkUCRvT13Q1mzi+Zz2LwRqNheclYPqaT2hdAV5UCZ4JW2s5N\n1/RkfFHoZiFj4nJ8k8Msfvk5mxlurcmGTwFlBzs4ThK1HaIevRsb6pTdySK1AduD\nb4gm7R7fjccN2Pw4K1reAM9t5yVl/3zCtE5bSOqtDM/44FyymZCcGZTyxmcsW1g0\nfK