"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/309364eac27ec86851a62c68f251adb071a59977","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKDMwOTM2NGVhYzI3ZWM4Njg1MWE2MmM2OGYyNTFhZGIwNzFhNTk5Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c","sha":"a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c"}],"sha":"309364eac27ec86851a62c68f251adb071a59977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/309364eac27ec86851a62c68f251adb071a59977"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T17:30:13Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T17:30:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): expose the deferred registration scope hook to non plugin consumers (#697)\n\n* feat(core): expose the deferred registration scope start as a runtime listener\n\nOnly routes and navigation items participate in a deferred registration\nrun. An application maintaining its own registry, filled from the same\ndeferred registration functions, had no way to join the run and no place\nto reset itself when a feature flag flipped off.\n\nAdds registerDeferredRegistrationScopeStartedListener /\nremoveDeferredRegistrationScopeStartedListener on Runtime. The callback\nreceives a DeferredRegistrationOperation (\"register\" | \"update\"), the\nsame value deferred registration functions already receive as their\nthird argument.\n\nThe listener set and the public API live on Runtime; the fan-out is\ntriggered by ReactRouterRuntime.startDeferredRegistrationScope calling\nthe protected _notifyDeferredRegistrationScopeStarted. Wrapping the\nabstract method instead would read better, but it requires renaming it,\nwhich is a major and silently breaks subclasses because\nnoImplicitOverride is off.\n\nModuleManager passes the operation explicitly rather than letting the\nruntime derive it from \"transactional\", which is a nav registry replay\nstrategy rather than a run identity. The new option is optional and\nfalls back to the derived value, so direct callers are unaffected.\n\nListener errors are logged, never propagated: startDeferredRegistration-\nScope is called before the try/finally that completes the scope, so an\nescaping error would leave the scope open for the lifetime of the\nruntime.\n\nOnly the started listener ships here; the completed listener is\ndeferred, as its buffering contract needs its own design pass.\n\nRefs #686. See ADR-0032.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(core): notify plugins when a deferred registration scope starts\n\nAdds one optional method to the abstract Plugin class, so a plugin owning a\nregistry that modules fill from their deferred registration functions can clear\nand replay it the way Squide already does for its navigation items.\n\nonDeferredRegistrationScopeStarted is executed when a run starts, before any\nmodule''s deferred registration function, and can return a completion function\nexecuted once the run has settled, while the runtime''s scope is still open. That\nordering is the point: the commit lands before the app router store notifies its\nsubscribers and before React re-renders, which the event bus cannot provide\nbecause useEnhancedReducerDispatch notifies subscribers before\nDeferredRegistrationsUpdateCompletedEvent, and because the initial deferred run\nhas no event bracket at all.\n\nModuleManager drives it from a shared #withDeferredRegistrationScope bracket.\nBoth public methods keep their existing bodies verbatim as the callback, so the\nconcurrent Promise.all of the initial run and the sequential Honeycomb-safe loop\nof an update run are unchanged.\n\nThe hook is optional and unimplemented on the base class, so no existing plugin\nneeds any change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix the Retype highlight offset and the agent skill bookkeeping\n\nThe !#7,10 annotation on the listener snippet pointed at a blank line and\na comment. Retype counts from the first line inside the fence, so the two\ncalls the snippet emphasizes are 8 and 11.\n\nEditing anything under agent-skills/ requires bumping the skill''s\nmetadata.version minor field, and runtime-api.md carries a table of\ncontents that the new Deferred Registration Scope section was missing\nfrom.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(core): document the plugin hook with JSDoc and trim inline comments\n\nThe hook and its option types are public API, so they get JSDoc rather than\ninline comments, which also surfaces them in tooling.\n\nThe scope bracket in ModuleManager keeps only the two comments that carry\nsomething the code cannot: why the plugins are notified before the modules run,\nand why the runtime scope must always be completed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(core): isolate a faulty plugin instead of failing the deferred registration run\n\nBoth changes come from review findings on the bootstrapping and rendering\nconsequences of letting a plugin error propagate.\n\nA throwing hook no longer aborts the run. It used to skip the module registries\nentirely, so LocalModuleRegistry never reached #setRegistrationStatus(\"ready\").\nisBootstrapping requires areModulesReady and useDeferredRegistrations doesn''t\ncatch the register() promise, so one faulty plugin pinned the application on its\nbootstrapping fallback for the whole session with only an unhandled rejection to\nshow for it. Each hook is now individually caught and logged with the plugin\nname, and the run carries on.\n\nA completion function error is no longer rethrown either. By that point the run\nhad succeeded and the navigation items were committed, so throwing aborted\nuseUpdateDeferredRegistrations before it dispatched \"deferred-registrations-updated\"\n— and useNavigationItems re-renders only off that dispatch, so the items that had\njust been committed were never rendered.\n\nBoth now match how a faulty module is already treated: Promise.allSettled\ncollects the error and the registry still goes \"ready\". Dropping the rethrow also\nremoves the result and completion-error bookkeeping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop ADR-0032 and state that new ADRs are not mandatory\n\nThis change adds an API and an option. It makes no architectural choice a\nfuture reader would reverse by accident, so it did not warrant a record,\nand the index every agent reads is worse for carrying one.\n\nCLAUDE.md now separates the two rules that were being conflated: reading\nthe ADR index stays mandatory, writing a new ADR does not, with a\nDo/Don''t pair marking the boundary and a default of putting the rationale\nin the changeset instead.\n\nThe rationale worth keeping -- why the event bus is not the channel, why\nthe abstract method is not wrapped, why there is no completed listener\nyet -- moves into agent-docs/design/deferred-registrations.md, which is\nwhere a reader working on deferred registrations already looks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: drop the changeset already consumed by #699\n\nIt rode in with the merge of #698''s feature branch, but #699 versioned\nthe packages from it on main. Keeping it would bump @squide/core a second\ntime for a release that already shipped.\n\n* fix: address the review round on the converged listeners\n\nFour real findings, all from the converged code rather than the design\nit replaced:\n\n- The doc examples buffered unconditionally, which the \"transactional\"\n  contract forbids: a non transactional run must write through, because\n  the modules become ready while its scope is still open. Copying that\n  example gave an empty registry for the whole first render pass, the\n  exact bug this API exists to prevent. Both examples now branch, the way\n  the plugin documentation already did.\n- The agent skill snippet also referenced an undeclared \"buffer\" and\n  mixed the two mutually exclusive strategies as if they were steps. It\n  is a file agents copy verbatim.\n- The completion error message still said \"plugin\", but the array now\n  holds the completion functions of both surfaces, so a faulty listener\n  was reported as a plugin failure. Nothing asserted the old string.\n- Runtime.test.ts restated the abstract surface the shared DummyRuntime\n  already maintains. The suite drives _notifyDeferredRegistrationScope-\n  Started directly and never calls the scope methods, so the shared\n  double fits as is.\n\nAlso pinned the \"new Set(...)\" copy in the fan-out. The existing test\ndisposed the first listener of itself, which a live Set iteration\nsurvives, so the copy could be deleted with the suite still green. The\nnew test disposes a *later* listener, which is the case that separates\nthem. Both that test and the error logging test were verified to fail\nwhen the code they pin is removed.\n\n* docs: routes do not participate in a deferred registration run\n\nOnly navigation items do. FireflyRuntime.registerRoute throws once the\nmodules are registered, and its message says so outright: \"Only\nnavigation items can be registered in a deferred registration function.\"\nADR-0001 states the same rule.\n\nThe sentence came from the issue this PR implements, and it was wrong\nthere too.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3a6ccaa1348eb07f94d71d1392d510288af7da7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/f3a6ccaa1348eb07f94d71d1392d510288af7da7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c","verification":{"payload":"tree f3a6ccaa1348eb07f94d71d1392d510288af7da7\nparent 8fad8ac44641d32ea7c544c61e8efb71843c7c6f\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787851813 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787851813 -0400\n\nfeat(core): expose the deferred registration scope hook to non plugin consumers (#697)\n\n* feat(core): expose the deferred registration scope start as a runtime listener\n\nOnly routes and navigation items participate in a deferred registration\nrun. An application maintaining its own registry, filled from the same\ndeferred registration functions, had no way to join the run and no place\nto reset itself when a feature flag flipped off.\n\nAdds registerDeferredRegistrationScopeStartedListener /\nremoveDeferredRegistrationScopeStartedListener on Runtime. The callback\nreceives a DeferredRegistrationOperation (\"register\" | \"update\"), the\nsame value deferred registration functions already receive as their\nthird argument.\n\nThe listener set and the public API live on Runtime; the fan-out is\ntriggered by ReactRouterRuntime.startDeferredRegistrationScope calling\nthe protected _notifyDeferredRegistrationScopeStarted. Wrapping the\nabstract method instead would read better, but it requires renaming it,\nwhich is a major and silently breaks subclasses because\nnoImplicitOverride is off.\n\nModuleManager passes the operation explicitly rather than letting the\nruntime derive it from \"transactional\", which is a nav registry replay\nstrategy rather than a run identity. The new option is optional and\nfalls back to the derived value, so direct callers are unaffected.\n\nListener errors are logged, never propagated: startDeferredRegistration-\nScope is called before the try/finally that completes the scope, so an\nescaping error would leave the scope open for the lifetime of the\nruntime.\n\nOnly the started listener ships here; the completed listener is\ndeferred, as its buffering contract needs its own design pass.\n\nRefs #686. See ADR-0032.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(core): notify plugins when a deferred registration scope starts\n\nAdds one optional method to the abstract Plugin class, so a plugin owning a\nregistry that modules fill from their deferred registration functions can clear\nand replay it the way Squide already does for its navigation items.\n\nonDeferredRegistrationScopeStarted is executed when a run starts, before any\nmodule''s deferred registration function, and can return a completion function\nexecuted once the run has settled, while the runtime''s scope is still open. That\nordering is the point: the commit lands before the app router store notifies its\nsubscribers and before React re-renders, which the event bus cannot provide\nbecause useEnhancedReducerDispatch notifies subscribers before\nDeferredRegistrationsUpdateCompletedEvent, and because the initial deferred run\nhas no event bracket at all.\n\nModuleManager drives it from a shared #withDeferredRegistrationScope bracket.\nBoth public methods keep their existing bodies verbatim as the callback, so the\nconcurrent Promise.all of the initial run and the sequential Honeycomb-safe loop\nof an update run are unchanged.\n\nThe hook is optional and unimplemented on the base class, so no existing plugin\nneeds any change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix the Retype highlight offset and the agent skill bookkeeping\n\nThe !#7,10 annotation on the listener snippet pointed at a blank line and\na comment. Retype counts from the first line inside the fence, so the two\ncalls the snippet emphasizes are 8 and 11.\n\nEditing anything under agent-skills/ requires bumping the skill''s\nmetadata.version minor field, and runtime-api.md carries a table of\ncontents that the new Deferred Registration Scope section was missing\nfrom.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(core): document the plugin hook with JSDoc and trim inline comments\n\nThe hook and its option types are public API, so they get JSDoc rather than\ninline comments, which also surfaces them in tooling.\n\nThe scope bracket in ModuleManager keeps only the two comments that carry\nsomething the code cannot: why the plugins are notified before the modules run,\nand why the runtime scope must always be completed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(core): isolate a faulty plugin instead of failing the deferred registration run\n\nBoth changes come from review findings on the bootstrapping and rendering\nconsequences of letting a plugin error propagate.\n\nA throwing hook no longer aborts the run. It used to skip the module registries\nentirely, so LocalModuleRegistry never reached #setRegistrationStatus(\"ready\").\nisBootstrapping requires areModulesReady and useDeferredRegistrations doesn''t\ncatch the register() promise, so one faulty plugin pinned the application on its\nbootstrapping fallback for the whole session with only an unhandled rejection to\nshow for it. Each hook is now individually caught and logged with the plugin\nname, and the run carries on.\n\nA completion function error is no longer rethrown either. By that point the run\nhad succeeded and the navigation items were committed, so throwing aborted\nuseUpdateDeferredRegistrations before it dispatched \"deferred-registrations-updated\"\n— and useNavigationItems re-renders only off that dispatch, so the items that had\njust been committed were never rendered.\n\nBoth now match how a faulty module is already treated: Promise.allSettled\ncollects the error and the registry still goes \"ready\". Dropping the rethrow also\nremoves the result and completion-error bookkeeping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop ADR-0032 and state that new ADRs are not mandatory\n\nThis change adds an API and an option. It makes no architectural choice a\nfuture reader would reverse by accident, so it did not warrant a record,\nand the index every agent reads is worse for carrying one.\n\nCLAUDE.md now separates the two rules that were being conflated: reading\nthe ADR index stays mandatory, writing a new ADR does not, with a\nDo/Don''t pair marking the boundary and a default of putting the rationale\nin the changeset instead.\n\nThe rationale worth keeping -- why the event bus is not the channel, why\nthe abstract method is not wrapped, why there is no completed listener\nyet -- moves into agent-docs/design/deferred-registrations.md, which is\nwhere a reader working on deferred registrations already looks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: drop the changeset already consumed by #699\n\nIt rode in with the merge of #698''s feature branch, but #699 versioned\nthe packages from it on main. Keeping it would bump @squide/core a second\ntime for a release that already shipped.\n\n* fix: address the review round on the converged listeners\n\nFour real findings, all from the converged code rather than the design\nit replaced:\n\n- The doc examples buffered unconditionally, which the \"transactional\"\n  contract forbids: a non transactional run must write through, because\n  the modules become ready while its scope is still open. Copying that\n  example gave an empty registry for the whole first render pass, the\n  exact bug this API exists to prevent. Both examples now branch, the way\n  the plugin documentation already did.\n- The agent skill snippet also referenced an undeclared \"buffer\" and\n  mixed the two mutually exclusive strategies as if they were steps. It\n  is a file agents copy verbatim.\n- The completion error message still said \"plugin\", but the array now\n  holds the completion functions of both surfaces, so a faulty listener\n  was reported as a plugin failure. Nothing asserted the old string.\n- Runtime.test.ts restated the abstract surface the shared DummyRuntime\n  already maintains. The suite drives _notifyDeferredRegistrationScope-\n  Started directly and never calls the scope methods, so the shared\n  double fits as is.\n\nAlso pinned the \"new Set(...)\" copy in the fan-out. The existing test\ndisposed the first listener of itself, which a live Set iteration\nsurvives, so the copy could be deleted with the suite still green. The\nnew test disposes a *later* listener, which is the case that separates\nthem. Both that test and the error logging test were verified to fail\nwhen the code they pin is removed.\n\n* docs: routes do not participate in a deferred registration run\n\nOnly navigation items do. FireflyRuntime.registerRoute throws once the\nmodules are registered, and its message says so outright: \"Only\nnavigation items can be registered in a deferred registration function.\"\nADR-0001 states the same rule.\n\nThe sentence came from the issue this PR implements, and it was wrong\nthere too.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkHQlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU8MQADVxe13wLcoQ/4iv3RZZjfN7\ndJcZYlzw1Lx/M1/a579Ll/GqEw/+LeTjAngRtHdPUZj42YQfVpKM5BVwqQntnyb4\n11KHeqE+fzCiF5vdNlJ2VXz8cl21Ew7QP+sQ/r6ZA8MYQcvacxdS0ar7Fm/B8gdL\nO8Uz3ZxG9w2U3NvbomKrbylYSMsTcP2NxnwpEkseanjLGZVTxGHHxdTlUVbLka0O\nfFicujmCAlJc+FdxXit3NHO3qm7whnn+kGz1o5FmY8wwbaV/I5g7y0nXK3Fv3rEN\n8XzWSu0O53MqoI/3+yyN5a/Zd9xjAlu9O2yBwYGmTbTSQYHXfVfzWi8KjMLosZ90\n/KDy0aEfsCkS4UgfZ1EwUX37i2A5V1WrwiKjpKYiyEGlkDZG8K07CgTOpRg573DI\npbiVLORTk1veJbJz0292NrXcINqEy/wj4VKzPAZAaZHG12loXb/fbfzh6/68zhoo\nvt5nzjJnFO5wMc9zSpdfh8+KSPzJBKnkPrGltnxwIIkEk2liFXIDsZF/WWFkoNU9\n/pLLxEfQxY3N0Q5fDSC5rWGit4B9N9XhEWCL7o3FUO8815EgOfvh5fPv/jFtKRqa\nDPq6909YXOfgorAaz/tuxibPftoFWsgJn/hctl3a6yjjAuR5lF9VXH/KfobIPbWv\nmuxCPzhSZLfY0ajKnB8c\n=qGKI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T17:30:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKGE2NmEwNGFmZTc1YjZjNTcwYjAyMDU5MDJlYjA4Y2YwMjhjYmE5NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/8fad8ac44641d32ea7c544c61e8efb71843c7c6f","sha":"8fad8ac44641d32ea7c544c61e8efb71843c7c6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/8fad8ac44641d32ea7c544c61e8efb71843c7c6f"}],"sha":"a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/a66a04afe75b6c570b0205902eb08cf028cba96c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/8fad8ac44641d32ea7c544c61e8efb71843c7c6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T16:19:19Z","email":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"claude[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T16:19:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(skill): sync workleap-squide skill with docs [skip ci] (#700)\n\nCo-authored-by: claude[bot] <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8891fede1d4f48a6c6729300900c05abf6a80aaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/8891fede1d4f48a6c6729300900c05abf6a80aaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/8fad8ac44641d32ea7c544c61e8efb71843c7c6f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8891fede1d4f48a6c6729300900c05abf6a80aaa\nparent 1d52524cd4adee7fdc4acf1c96f3e6982f1ca392\nauthor claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787847559 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787847559 -0400\n\nchore(skill): sync workleap-squide skill with docs [skip ci] (#700)\n\nCo-authored-by: claude[bot] <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkGOHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFOkQAArP+XxALlWnTZQAk81Bh1mE\nX/fwK9/Fgvn2AYHKuDyTO5FXzCdXe+vuMD9TBBS+LsrkFvzY3P4PuxyBq5Wv2uL9\nlzuDM0w3YoHaXdNMqzPE7kdXOCVxFrp1/kG4N2NSth9iCHExsN625dGpLV/L87KB\nutPeDx+5LSv3e6TeBr6wc+42YvrHyoJDR/zYOisp/x+yGqraOI/LLejgUeIdurdU\naMeawHf5xNTnMeCWWGWL52RLlqhPcxm/n8MlbXh7QVRBHqp5u4