_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/1d52524cd4adee7fdc4acf1c96f3e6982f1ca392","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKDFkNTI1MjRjZDRhZGVlN2ZkYzRhY2YxYzk2ZjNlNjk4MmYxY2EzOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e","sha":"c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e"}],"sha":"1d52524cd4adee7fdc4acf1c96f3e6982f1ca392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/1d52524cd4adee7fdc4acf1c96f3e6982f1ca392"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T15:42:26Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T15:42:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): notify plugins when a deferred registration scope starts (#698)\n\n* feat(core): notify plugins when a deferred registration scope starts\n\nAdds one optional method to the abstract Plugin class, so a plugin owning a\nregistry that modules fill from their deferred registration functions can clear\nand replay it the way Squide already does for its navigation items.\n\nonDeferredRegistrationScopeStarted is executed when a run starts, before any\nmodule''s deferred registration function, and can return a completion function\nexecuted once the run has settled, while the runtime''s scope is still open. That\nordering is the point: the commit lands before the app router store notifies its\nsubscribers and before React re-renders, which the event bus cannot provide\nbecause useEnhancedReducerDispatch notifies subscribers before\nDeferredRegistrationsUpdateCompletedEvent, and because the initial deferred run\nhas no event bracket at all.\n\nModuleManager drives it from a shared #withDeferredRegistrationScope bracket.\nBoth public methods keep their existing bodies verbatim as the callback, so the\nconcurrent Promise.all of the initial run and the sequential Honeycomb-safe loop\nof an update run are unchanged.\n\nThe hook is optional and unimplemented on the base class, so no existing plugin\nneeds any change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(core): document the plugin hook with JSDoc and trim inline comments\n\nThe hook and its option types are public API, so they get JSDoc rather than\ninline comments, which also surfaces them in tooling.\n\nThe scope bracket in ModuleManager keeps only the two comments that carry\nsomething the code cannot: why the plugins are notified before the modules run,\nand why the runtime scope must always be completed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(core): isolate a faulty plugin instead of failing the deferred registration run\n\nBoth changes come from review findings on the bootstrapping and rendering\nconsequences of letting a plugin error propagate.\n\nA throwing hook no longer aborts the run. It used to skip the module registries\nentirely, so LocalModuleRegistry never reached #setRegistrationStatus(\"ready\").\nisBootstrapping requires areModulesReady and useDeferredRegistrations doesn''t\ncatch the register() promise, so one faulty plugin pinned the application on its\nbootstrapping fallback for the whole session with only an unhandled rejection to\nshow for it. Each hook is now individually caught and logged with the plugin\nname, and the run carries on.\n\nA completion function error is no longer rethrown either. By that point the run\nhad succeeded and the navigation items were committed, so throwing aborted\nuseUpdateDeferredRegistrations before it dispatched \"deferred-registrations-updated\"\n— and useNavigationItems re-renders only off that dispatch, so the items that had\njust been committed were never rendered.\n\nBoth now match how a faulty module is already treated: Promise.allSettled\ncollects the error and the registry still goes \"ready\". Dropping the rethrow also\nremoves the result and completion-error bookkeeping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(core): correct the no-rollback wording for a failing module\n\n\"A failing module silently drops its own entries for that run\" implied a\nper-module atomicity that doesn''t exist. LocalModuleRegistry wraps each module''s\ndeferred registration in a try/catch that only collects a ModuleRegistrationError,\nso a module that throws part way through keeps whatever it already registered, in\nthe navigation registry and in a plugin''s buffer alike.\n\nA plugin author could have read the old wording as a guarantee and skipped\nhandling half-registered entries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"632c00256c8aec9103e54dbbdaa7e5b4ef04a0f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/632c00256c8aec9103e54dbbdaa7e5b4ef04a0f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e","verification":{"payload":"tree 632c00256c8aec9103e54dbbdaa7e5b4ef04a0f9\nparent e86521c380714f574d20c9a55da173cf2f87416a\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787845346 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787845346 -0400\n\nfeat(core): notify plugins when a deferred registration scope starts (#698)\n\n* feat(core): notify plugins when a deferred registration scope starts\n\nAdds one optional method to the abstract Plugin class, so a plugin owning a\nregistry that modules fill from their deferred registration functions can clear\nand replay it the way Squide already does for its navigation items.\n\nonDeferredRegistrationScopeStarted is executed when a run starts, before any\nmodule''s deferred registration function, and can return a completion function\nexecuted once the run has settled, while the runtime''s scope is still open. That\nordering is the point: the commit lands before the app router store notifies its\nsubscribers and before React re-renders, which the event bus cannot provide\nbecause useEnhancedReducerDispatch notifies subscribers before\nDeferredRegistrationsUpdateCompletedEvent, and because the initial deferred run\nhas no event bracket at all.\n\nModuleManager drives it from a shared #withDeferredRegistrationScope bracket.\nBoth public methods keep their existing bodies verbatim as the callback, so the\nconcurrent Promise.all of the initial run and the sequential Honeycomb-safe loop\nof an update run are unchanged.\n\nThe hook is optional and unimplemented on the base class, so no existing plugin\nneeds any change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(core): document the plugin hook with JSDoc and trim inline comments\n\nThe hook and its option types are public API, so they get JSDoc rather than\ninline comments, which also surfaces them in tooling.\n\nThe scope bracket in ModuleManager keeps only the two comments that carry\nsomething the code cannot: why the plugins are notified before the modules run,\nand why the runtime scope must always be completed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(core): isolate a faulty plugin instead of failing the deferred registration run\n\nBoth changes come from review findings on the bootstrapping and rendering\nconsequences of letting a plugin error propagate.\n\nA throwing hook no longer aborts the run. It used to skip the module registries\nentirely, so LocalModuleRegistry never reached #setRegistrationStatus(\"ready\").\nisBootstrapping requires areModulesReady and useDeferredRegistrations doesn''t\ncatch the register() promise, so one faulty plugin pinned the application on its\nbootstrapping fallback for the whole session with only an unhandled rejection to\nshow for it. Each hook is now individually caught and logged with the plugin\nname, and the run carries on.\n\nA completion function error is no longer rethrown either. By that point the run\nhad succeeded and the navigation items were committed, so throwing aborted\nuseUpdateDeferredRegistrations before it dispatched \"deferred-registrations-updated\"\n— and useNavigationItems re-renders only off that dispatch, so the items that had\njust been committed were never rendered.\n\nBoth now match how a faulty module is already treated: Promise.allSettled\ncollects the error and the registry still goes \"ready\". Dropping the rethrow also\nremoves the result and completion-error bookkeeping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(core): correct the no-rollback wording for a failing module\n\n\"A failing module silently drops its own entries for that run\" implied a\nper-module atomicity that doesn''t exist. LocalModuleRegistry wraps each module''s\ndeferred registration in a try/catch that only collects a ModuleRegistrationError,\nso a module that throws part way through keeps whatever it already registered, in\nthe navigation registry and in a plugin''s buffer alike.\n\nA plugin author could have read the old wording as a guarantee and skipped\nhandling half-registered entries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkFriCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKWIQAJlxNmTLT3LUYuElr+ZGMnnQ\nARtr2bODgFL6x3Bu+U7qnzcvUMSEJpmObHQWDb3gmae52bjOLbBEWeasUzvXsGor\nVwmSKTYxyJ9YTbuXaOrcB8QSyTQYfP/as/XRWQsYC+eieY41AM9v6l/9GYIgs9vS\n335G534nz0IZlt5xFQoHNdt/H2P5h68gELyLQCjXwsymxHPnS+GD72AOHj2itd+n\nnYGDam9XA7uhVa9mVzzLiEEA71Oz1rvbQw3fsRevQYZ0E6Mwo5P5dxaDjmyi2Qjk\nSqmeTivuNG68Zp8QeRFuIbjRO4AGkhVMcsYB06lgcAAGWd0m5o2oDps2F8PFJJm4\nyjqBxMER1uBjtEaJxl1HhSQzZIGY8WOotYI9WLc6G7BO+juZ8UpAEJzyoo+FOXs1\nooee34peyIZ36ahHZoHgXP3oJRX0uOXLDufRF/zXPkxPliUhiU2A0B1qe9CJmHEE\nOX+PHYNV4jNLjJ4UdkyuKXCOz9v1ewA8p8T2Fuj631zciXDu+Pud0wFetJLW2gQ3\nufREsBsMUCPzab2tH88uOji9hYiU6r9CBsGvsll/6MRSaWKskP69IArmWLA9Erxt\njwzsqFn2Eu3d+huG8Ief1DfmxHYDITPHqDlgXmdqMkeIGbQ6+sfIsDquDaFjqKLo\nVV4SLZDuy7sY9EQJLlvv\n=S+pa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T15:42:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKGM5MmJkZmMxNzAxNWZkNTI0Y2I0MGVjY2MwNmM5NGM2Y2Y2OTU0OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/e86521c380714f574d20c9a55da173cf2f87416a","sha":"e86521c380714f574d20c9a55da173cf2f87416a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/e86521c380714f574d20c9a55da173cf2f87416a"}],"sha":"c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/c92bdfc17015fd524cb40eccc06c94c6cf69548e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1236702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","id":209825114,"login":"claude[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODIGtWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claud