pi.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/070a6fd1b05aa09e7970994613a2c1dfed7288f9","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKDA3MGE2ZmQxYjA1YWEwOWU3OTcwOTk0NjEzYTJjMWRmZWQ3Mjg4Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/e6585374d2efbf593b6f0b859bad310e1700537c","sha":"e6585374d2efbf593b6f0b859bad310e1700537c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/e6585374d2efbf593b6f0b859bad310e1700537c"}],"sha":"070a6fd1b05aa09e7970994613a2c1dfed7288f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/070a6fd1b05aa09e7970994613a2c1dfed7288f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/e6585374d2efbf593b6f0b859bad310e1700537c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T04:38:34Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T04:38:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(react-router)!: rename $meta to $context, and fix the priority comparator docs (#693)\n\n* docs: a priority comparator runs on $priority, not the priority render prop\n\nBoth the public reference and the agent skill showed a comparator over\n`priority`, the render prop. There is no array of render props to sort:\n`renderItem` receives one item at a time and `renderSection` receives a\nsingle already-rendered `section: ReactNode`\n(useRenderedNavigationItems.tsx:20,113). The only comparator a consumer\ncan write runs over the items from `useNavigationItems`, before they\nreach the hook, where the property is `$priority`.\n\nFollowing the old text produced a compile error rather than the sort it\npromised, and the `TS18048` it predicted was not the error you got.\nVerified against `RootNavigationItem[]` with `npx tsgo --noEmit`:\n\n  (y.priority ?? 0) - (x.priority ?? 0)    TS2551 \"Did you mean ''$priority''?\"\n  y.$priority - x.$priority                TS18048\n  (y.$priority ?? 0) - (x.$priority ?? 0)  clean\n\nThe `NaN` paragraph is unchanged and stays accurate: it describes what\nhappens once the type error is cast away.\n\nRaised in review on #687:\nhttps://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/pull/687#discussion_r3868165771\nhttps://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/pull/687#discussion_r3868166185\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(react-router)!: rename the navigation item $meta option to $context\n\n$meta is the channel for values the code rendering the menu reads rather\nthan forwards, as opposed to $additionalProps, which is spread onto the\ncomponent. Only the name changes; behavior is identical.\n\nRenames all four source sites together, since missing one fails quietly\nrather than loudly: $context would fall into the linkProps rest, be\nremoved by stripMetadataProps (which filters generically on the \"$\"\nprefix, NavigationItemRegistry.ts is not consulted), and the render prop\nwould silently be {}. toMenuProps has no rest element at all.\n\nsamples/endpoints/shell/src/AuthenticatedLayout.tsx reads the render\nprop but registers no $meta anywhere, so a \"$meta\" search never reaches\nit. Storybook''s `const meta` convention appears ~30 times across the\ndocs and skill and is untouched.\n\nShipped as a minor, not a major: $meta landed two days ago in 9.1.0\n(#665) and has no known adopters. Same call as 6.3.0 for $name -> $id\n(#206), which the changeset cites. No deprecated alias — supporting both\nwould mean `context: $context ?? $meta ?? {}`, entrenching the name\nbeing removed.\n\nThe name collides with two existing meanings of \"context\" in Squide: the\nmodule registration context (TContext in initializeFirefly.ts:24-50) and\nReact context (RuntimeContext, AppRouterContext). Chosen with that\nknown. The reference, the design doc and the skill each say what\n$context is not, and NavigationItemRegistry.ts carries the same note at\nthe declaration.\n\nADR-0018 is amended in place rather than superseded: it named $meta in\nits Options Considered and Evidence sections, which are factual claims\nabout what the code declares. The $-prefix decision itself is untouched.\n\nCHANGELOGs are left alone: 9.1.0 really did ship $meta.\n\nturbo typecheck 35/35, lint 71/71, test 11/11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address bot review on #693\n\nAll seven findings were legit; each verified against the source before\napplying.\n\nCopy before sorting. useNavigationItems() -> getNavigationItems() ->\ngetItems(menuId) -> #memoizedGetItems(menuId) hands back the same array\ninstance on every call (NavigationItemRegistry.ts:206-207,419-421), so\nthe `navigationItems.sort(...)` I wrote mutated the registry for every\nconsumer of that menu — and did not even work for the caller, since the\nreference never changes and the hook''s useMemo does not re-run. The\ncomplete example 20 lines below already did `[...items].sort(...)`, so\nthe warning contradicted the code it introduced. Fixed in the reference\nand in the skill.\n\nThe changeset now bumps @squide/firefly too. packages/firefly/src/index.ts:48\nis `export * from \"@squide/react-router\"` and every doc and sample here\nimports from @squide/firefly, so the rename lands on its public surface.\nThe changeset that added $meta (#665) bumped both packages; with only\nreact-router listed, firefly would ship the rename as a patch whose\nchangelog says nothing but \"Updated dependencies\".\n\nFireflyRuntime.md still called it metadata in the heading and the note\nunder the example, which made it the only reference page presenting\n$context as metadata. Renamed, as register-nav-items.md already was. No\ninbound links use the old anchor.\n\nBoth MessagePage samples rendered \"custom metadata ($context)\" to the\nuser, pairing the two words the rename separates. Also fixes the\npre-existing \"use\" -> \"uses\" on the line.\n\nturbo typecheck + lint + test: 82/82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: qualify the $meta version range by package, and drop a relative date\n\nSecond bot review round on #693. All three findings legit.\n\n\"9.1.0-9.6.0\" is @squide/react-router numbering, but every example in\nthe skill and the design doc imports from @squide/firefly, which is at\n18.7.0. An agent migrating an app pinned to @squide/firefly@18.5.0 would\ncompare it against 9.1.0-9.6.0, conclude the note does not apply, and\nsay $context is already available there. Verified $meta shipped as\nfirefly 18.2.0 (packages/firefly/CHANGELOG.md:172-176, #665), so both\nranges are now named.\n\nThe changeset carried the same ambiguity in a spot the review did not\nflag: its body is copied verbatim into packages/firefly/CHANGELOG.md,\nwhere \"added in 9.1.0\" is not a number that reader has. Both packages\nnamed there too.\n\nAlso replaced \"shipped two days ago\" with the date. A changeset body\nbecomes a permanent CHANGELOG entry, so a relative date is wrong the day\nafter it is written and worse every day the PR sits.\n\nturbo typecheck + lint + test: 82/82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: annotate the comparator params so the cited TS18048 is real\n\nDefect I introduced resolving the merge with main. Dropping\n`items.sort(...)` was right — post-#688 the hook sorts every array it\nreceives, so there is no array of render props to sort — but it also\nremoved the only thing giving x and y a contextual type. As bare arrow\nexpressions their params are implicitly any, so the snippet produced\nTS7006 and the subtraction type-checked fine, making the cited TS18048\nwrong.\n\nVerified with npx tsgo --noEmit against NavigationLinkRenderProps:\n\n  (x, y) => y.priority - x.priority                    TS7006 x2, no TS18048\n  (x: NLRP, y: NLRP) => y.priority - x.priority        TS18048\n  (x: NLRP, y: NLRP) => (y.priority ?? 0) - (...)      clean\n\nturbo typecheck + lint + test: 82/82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18c50c623be14741cb392bcd501b40a0adbaccd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/18c50c623be14741cb392bcd501b40a0adbaccd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/e6585374d2efbf593b6f0b859bad310e1700537c","verification":{"payload":"tree 18c50c623be14741cb392bcd501b40a0adbaccd0\nparent bbfc988c2e136cbf9ffac7f1f6cbfc1a641a7156\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787805514 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787805514 -0400\n\nfeat(react-router)!: rename $meta to $context, and fix the priority comparator docs (#693)\n\n* docs: a priority comparator runs on $priority, not the priority render prop\n\nBoth the public reference and the agent skill showed a comparator over\n`priority`, the render prop. There is no array of render props to sort:\n`renderItem` receives one item at a time and `renderSection` receives a\nsingle already-rendered `section: ReactNode`\n(useRenderedNavigationItems.tsx:20,113). The only comparator a consumer\ncan write runs over the items from `useNavigationItems`, before they\nreach the hook, where the property is `$priority`.\n\nFollowing the old text produced a compile error rather than the sort it\npromised, and the `TS18048` it predicted was not the error you got.\nVerified against `RootNavigationItem[]` with `npx tsgo --noEmit`:\n\n  (y.priority ?? 0) - (x.priority ?? 0)    TS2551 \"Did you mean ''$priority''?\"\n  y.$priority - x.$priority                TS18048\n  (y.$priority ?? 0) - (x.$priority ?? 0)  clean\n\nThe `NaN` paragraph is unchanged and stays accurate: it describes what\nhappens once the type error is cast away.\n\nRaised in review on #687:\nhttps://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/pull/687#discussion_r3868165771\nhttps://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/pull/687#discussion_r3868166185\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(react-router)!: rename the navigation item $meta option to $context\n\n$meta is the channel for values the code rendering the menu reads rather\nthan forwards, as opposed to $additionalProps, which is spread onto the\ncomponent. Only the name changes; behavior is identical.\n\nRenames all four source sites together, since missing one fails quietly\nrather than loudly: $context would fall into the linkProps rest, be\nremoved by stripMetadataProps (which filters generically on the \"$\"\nprefix, NavigationItemRegistry.ts is not consulted), and the render prop\nwould silently be {}. toMenuProps has no rest element at all.\n\nsamples/endpoints/shell/src/AuthenticatedLayout.tsx reads the render\nprop but registers no $meta anywhere, so a \"$meta\" search never reaches\nit. Storybook''s `const meta` convention appears ~30 times across the\ndocs and skill and is untouched.\n\nShipped as a minor, not a major: $meta landed two days ago in 9.1.0\n(#665) and has no known adopters. Same call as 6.3.0 for $name -> $id\n(#206), which the changeset cites. No deprecated alias — supporting both\nwould mean `context: $context ?? $meta ?? {}`, entrenching the name\nbeing removed.\n\nThe name collides with two existing meanings of \"context\" in Squide: the\nmodule registration context (TContext in initializeFirefly.ts:24-50) and\nReact context (RuntimeContext, AppRouterContext). Chosen with that\nknown. The reference, the design doc and the skill each say what\n$context is not, and NavigationItemRegistry.ts carries the same note at\nthe declaration.\n\nADR-0018 is amended in place rather than superseded: it named $meta in\nits Options Considered and Evidence sections, which are factual claims\nabout what the code declares. The $-prefix decision itself is untouched.\n\nCHANGELOGs are left alone: 9.1.0 really did ship $meta.\n\nturbo typecheck 35/35, lint 71/71, test 11/11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address bot review on #693\n\nAll seven findings were legit; each verified against the source before\napplying.\n\nCopy before sorting. useNavigationItems() -> getNavigationItems() ->\ngetItems(menuId) -> #memoizedGetItems(menuId) hands back the same array\ninstance on every call (NavigationItemRegistry.ts:206-207,419-421), so\nthe `navigationItems.sort(...)` I wrote mutated the registry for every\nconsumer of that menu — and did not even work for the caller, since the\nreference never changes and the hook''s useMemo does not re-run. The\ncomplete example 20 lines below already did `[...items].sort(...)`, so\nthe warning contradicted the code it introduced. Fixed in the reference\nand in the skill.\n\nThe changeset now bumps @squide/firefly too. packages/firefly/src/index.ts:48\nis `export * from \"@squide/react-router\"` and every doc and sample here\nimports from @squide/firefly, so the rename lands on its public surface.\nThe changeset that added $meta (#665) bumped both packages; with only\nreact-router listed, firefly would ship the rename as a patch whose\nchangelog says nothing but \"Updated dependencies\".\n\nFireflyRuntime.md still called it metadata in the heading and the note\nunder the example, which made it the only reference page presenting\n$context as metadata. Renamed, as register-nav-items.md already was. No\ninbound links use the old anchor.\n\nBoth MessagePage samples rendered \"custom metadata ($context)\" to the\nuser, pairing the two words the rename separates. Also fixes the\npre-existing \"use\" -> \"uses\" on the line.\n\nturbo typecheck + lint + test: 82/82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: qualify the $meta version range by package, and drop a relative date\n\nSecond bot review round on #693. All three findings legit.\n\n\"9.1.0-9.6.0\" is @squide/react-router numbering, but every example in\nthe skill and the design doc imports from @squide/firefly, which is at\n18.7.0. An agent migrating an app pinned to @squide/firefly@18.5.0 would\ncompare it against 9.1.0-9.6.0, conclude the note does not apply, and\nsay $context is already available there. Verified $meta shipped as\nfirefly 18.2.0 (packages/firefly/CHANGELOG.md:172-176, #665), so both\nranges are now named.\n\nThe changeset carried the same ambiguity in a spot the review did not\nflag: its body is copied verbatim into packages/firefly/CHANGELOG.md,\nwhere \"added in 9.1.0\" is not a number that reader has. Both packages\nnamed there too.\n\nAlso replaced \"shipped two days ago\" with the date. A changeset body\nbecomes a permanent CHANGELOG entry, so a relative date is wrong the day\nafter it is written and worse every day the PR sits.\n\nturbo typecheck + lint + test: 82/82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: annotate the comparator params so the cited TS18048 is real\n\nDefect I introduced resolving the merge with main. Dropping\n`items.sort(...)` was right — post-#688 the hook sorts every array it\nreceives, so there is no array of render props to sort — but it also\nremoved the only thing giving x and y a contextual type. As bare arrow\nexpressions their params are implicitly any, so the snippet produced\nTS7006 and the subtraction type-checked fine, making the cited TS18048\nwrong.\n\nVerified with npx tsgo --noEmit against NavigationLinkRenderProps:\n\n  (x, y) => y.priority - x.priority                    TS7006 x2, no TS18048\n  (x: NLRP, y: NLRP) => y.priority - x.priority        TS18048\n  (x: NLRP, y: NLRP) => (y.priority ?? 0) - (...)      clean\n\nturbo typecheck + lint + test: 82/82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj79KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgLIQAC29IOnvC7e7/zmMky6J367p\nEHAJrACbzDS1gz2s+Lt3tTzZYk9veT0I9rJvhRzYdGVzxBiuZ7C+yV0T2RkanPya\nzoOOWOHFTL5qGq6uayvG9nRvCcUiay2V/xowmK7/MtCkZ1jz9HUndHZ6NyHU4GgG\nUNe09WMPvs5Ce2Y0Q4zNlAYM3he4jMvF0FQv5ZoUnZ/ErZ7PTFbLTF3FkPjt5/cX\nzUfLWaCx68ui1iIYfzfwboXpdFgu7Kk+FNzoKWtE5oN0vBKbz3WAck7qV05hrOLw\nUwjunM9WvRZSrzXhr/Ivs5MqNUMIwK6vLoRHWqZLXwCnpf1wHtL0+jmsw67+hrH2\nFg+bAjw99pC79CXyB+g+MqAIP7d3S+0WIHMULCUA3dPfI7f7dXOi1ZwL1MwF0iKH\nLu99QgR56/asLO3dHRt9uMWnln1K7wBIFRHsGky2yEB1IzFqCzV1dWGJwdrYhMoD\nSCYu33pakwdShVENlnTaCbjm0aNVPmDW0W2rlruqNF0FYKA/JYkCgM8k2vCOmj+z\npWL0BgvRHSGEbEukMMvSBKVPV3Scw56QzSpghZvdhwRfV67UzfM73Sogb9QCN0/w\ncpy3xHsP6C3Qr3BzkB9SvonhienBXiNF6dQkHz8TIcIeZQLofZKrmFdWhUBW6tCR\nxd3FWR59BbqKBWT09YRJ\n=mTDM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T04:38:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.gith