d-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct what a NaN comparator actually does\n\n\"the sort silently no-ops\" was wrong twice over.\n\nA comparator returning NaN is coerced to +0 per CompareArrayElements, so it\nreads as \"these two are equal\". That makes the comparator inconsistent and the\nitems come back partially reordered — not left alone. A reader debugging a\nscrambled menu would have looked in the wrong place.\n\nIt is also not silent: \"priority\" is optional, so \"y.priority - x.priority\" is\na TS18048 error before it ever runs. The type system is the first line of\ndefense here, which is worth saying rather than hiding.\n\nCorrected in the public doc and in the skill, where an agent would have\nrepeated the claim.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(adr): the numbering rule has to account for in-flight records\n\n\"Take the highest in this folder and increment\" only sees \"main\", so it hands\nout a number another open PR already claimed. It has now produced a wrong\nreview finding three times, twice on this PR alone: 0022 belongs to the open\n#684 and 0023-0025 to the \"spike/registry-projection\" branch, none of which\nthis folder shows.\n\nNumbers are claimed when an ADR is written, not when it merges. The rule now\nsays to check unmerged branches and gives the command, and says explicitly\nthat a gap is the expected outcome rather than a mistake to correct — the gap\nis what stops two PRs from colliding on the same number.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: this is a feature, not a regression fix\n\nI claimed #665 removed an intended forwarding channel. It did not, and the\nhistory says so plainly.\n\n\"a39c15176\", the first version of this package, sorted the array it received\nand then stripped the property before recursing:\n\n    .sort(/* by priority */)\n    // priority is intentionally omitted.\n    .map(({ priority, ...itemProps }) => ({ ...itemProps }));\n\nThat strip survived two years and every refactor — \"git show 7925636fb^\" has\nit verbatim, comment included, immediately before the \"$meta\" PR. #665 removed\nthe strip and put \"stripMetadataProps\" in its place. There was never a\nforwarding channel to break.\n\nThe only way \"$priority\" ever reached a renderer was as a stray key inside\n\"linkProps\", and only on nested items, since the root-level strip did not apply\nto \"children\". From there it was spread onto the DOM Link as an invalid\n\"$priority\" attribute. That is the leak \"stripMetadataProps\" was written to\nclose, not a feature it removed.\n\nSo the changeset, the ADR and the test comment all described a regression that\ndid not happen. Rewritten.\n\nThe real reason this change is wanted is in the rewritten ADR: the root-only\nscope was coherent while a section''s \"children\" were always one array literal\nauthored in one place. The \"sectionId\" option made \"children\" a cross-module\ncomposition point, which is precisely what \"$priority\" exists for at the root,\nand did not revisit the sort. Modules register concurrently, so the resulting\norder is a function of network timing rather than authorship, with no lever to\ncorrect it.\n\nADR-0026 now records the whole decision — sort at every depth *and* forward the\nvalue — rather than a position already superseded before it landed. Renamed to\nmatch. The sort ships separately so a behavior change is not bundled with an\nadditive one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(adr): the index row must not claim behavior this PR does not ship\n\nThe row said \"$priority\" orders items at every depth. This PR only forwards\nthe value; the sort lands separately, which the ADR itself says. index.md\ndescribes itself as the quick reference where each line stands alone, and\nCLAUDE.md points agents at it before an API change, so an overstated row here\nmakes an agent assert the thing the rest of the PR carefully withdraws. The\ndesign doc updated in this same PR said the opposite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(adr): drop ADR-0026\n\nNot needed. The change is a forwarding fix plus a type move, both of which the\nchangeset and the code comments already explain, and the archaeology that\njustified a record is in the commit history where it is discoverable.\n\nRemoves the ADR, its index row, and the changeset''s reference to it. Verified no\nreference remains in \".changeset\", \"agent-docs\", \"docs\", \"agent-skills\" or the\nreact-router sources and tests. \"agent-docs/adr/index.md\" ends at 0020 again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj5rGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdCIQAJFc1DuQ0b43KTWrkk6KOU6O\nV7w0OkLgGQmUkUViqqkKK5HCmvgchHp/Ec9rFbY0Sntpal1mSCBZsKGu2BF4O0Bl\naU0VqxdecI5QYWhZiqiJN5mSzfdX/X/juj1E5n5ZtoAlFFvQVD5AGV1uiTbYFxhP\nNna2p+A/TwVWyCFP3fEi/fRMkyLxFCYX9UvG4XCdqMqG+nhmlkVTB4PyvbHwvkXa\nMmes0nPUYQF6WyU+4J2Df/C1Lgn9ANmHcZceF7U/yiCvnLQhEFRGyjn1w8kI++iX\nwpDwc3DgKBWtI7ucNFzjHvUiaKko+3vorw6IDS5zIFcdkDhi78dqmo32EqcLTb9V\nVENLRufqF6jQyo6/X4cDR3nfJe2VbtvIq7x1hIaQ6XO3kxiXX9LFt1JpG7p0vI5V\npa0/0Mfc3FH5d8KUFp+evX8eyYg2vbDFij2j4KpOn4/arYWYOTW4h8WYPS6CDWtr\nE5NjF/awYa7+gQ996wdk/hnSPedq0GC2VnK9RvMc0Hdtgh3Vacjizi4gjCseNT/0\nXD4mEZQcawJwLIy/kdIWqu8LbbLOe7DNmS9GX0+XfnjmithlLafcuLRpgE5NrJDV\ngKyquf9QeSYYP3azvQrMespYgFLqd/3uWfEnalBYl0w7X6oUoQ2X04Ws0mycfPwS\nZeyNM/3hF+2Nm47Zvyl2\n=tFzk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T02:02:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.git