R3Yhxku1dhF2rLXRTvOSj4g3OfqC3qoZ4SzwKOKW6lkZx/ZaDRXrHr7b\nNhhc8Ck7qejUDh+t9vqvsnknTwqi3oWcqrCpuSqkw5w46eDHZreKSsZV5PeP6JVi\njyRbdiHqoG72Fi0apVif\n=99RO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T20:00:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/2014eb210c02101bde20daf9a311e71fc4d2d83c","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKDIwMTRlYjIxMGMwMjEwMWJkZTIwZGFmOWEzMTFlNzFmYzRkMmQ4M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/b8bfd7caf4286c5cffbf449d2ea211ae49c5b8dc","sha":"b8bfd7caf4286c5cffbf449d2ea211ae49c5b8dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/b8bfd7caf4286c5cffbf449d2ea211ae49c5b8dc"}],"sha":"2014eb210c02101bde20daf9a311e71fc4d2d83c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/2014eb210c02101bde20daf9a311e71fc4d2d83c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/b8bfd7caf4286c5cffbf449d2ea211ae49c5b8dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:56:05Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:56:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): stop reporting a failed registration as successful (#682)\n\n* fix(core): stop reporting a failed registration as successful\n\nThe \"Successfully registered/updated ...\" log sat after the try/catch in\nfive of the six module registration paths, so it also ran on the error\npath: the failure was logged, the scope was ended red, a\nModuleRegistrationError was pushed, and then the success log was written\nand the scope ended a second time.\n\nBoth loggers that implement a logger scope today, @workleap/logging and\n@workleap/logrocket, buffer a scope''s logs and flush them from end(), and\nboth ignore a second end() call, so the stray log was queued into an\nalready ended scope and discarded. The defect is invisible with every\nlogger that currently exists and surfaces only for one that writes each\nlog as it is called. Verified against both dists rather than assumed.\n\nThe success log and its end() move inside the try, which is the shape\nRemoteModuleRegistry.registerModules already used. That site was already\ncorrect and is left untouched.\n\nThe tests record through a write-through logger that also records scope\nends as \"end:<color>\". The moved end() is half the fix, and asserting on\nlog text alone does not observe it: deleting every green end() left the\nwhole suite passing. All six sites are now covered, including the\nreference one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: pin the registration logging invariants across every failure mask\n\nThe cherry-picked fix ships example-based tests: one failing module next\nto one succeeding one, per loop. That pins the defect that was found. It\ndoes not pin the property, so the next rearrangement of these loops has\none example standing between it and a silent regression.\n\nThese assert the structure instead. For each of the 6 registration loops,\nall 16 combinations of which of 4 modules fail, reduced to one comparison:\n\n- a success line appears exactly as many times as the loop counted a\n  completion\n- every scope ends exactly once\n- no scope reports both outcomes, or neither\n- the colour of a scope''s end agrees with its outcome\n\nAttribution per scope is what the flat RecordingLogger cannot give. The\ntotals alone pass a mask with as many successes as failures while a\nsuccess line sits in a scope that failed, which is precisely the defect.\n\nMutation-verified, since none of this is worth anything if it cannot fail:\n\n- success log moved back below the try/catch — kills 15/16 masks; the\n  survivor is \"no module fails\", which takes no error path\n- green end() deleted — kills 15/16; the survivor is \"every module\n  fails\", where every scope already ends red exactly once so a missing\n  green end is unobservable\n- same move applied to RemoteModuleRegistry.registerModules, the site\n  that was already correct and that the other five were changed to match\n  — kills 15/16, so that coverage is not vacuous\n\nThe two local mutations are complementary: every mask is killed by at\nleast one. Mutations were run in a separate worktree, not here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(changeset): stop the first sentence reading as an output change\n\n\"reporting a failed registration as successfully registered\" describes\nthe code accurately but reads, on its own, as though a console line\nchanged. Nothing a consumer sees changed, and the second paragraph\nalready says so — the first sentence should not undo it.\n\nReworded to describe the code path rather than an outcome.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: share DummyRuntime instead of copying it per test file\n\nDummyRuntime was defined inline in four test files, byte-identical in all\nfour (868 bytes each). Two copies per package drift the moment Runtime\ngains an abstract member, and the compiler only reports whichever file it\ncompiles first.\n\nExtracted to packages/core/tests/DummyRuntime.ts and to the module\nfederation package''s existing tests/utils.ts, and imported from both test\nfiles in each package. Net -123 lines.\n\nThe cross-package half is left alone: sharing between @squide/core and\n@squide/firefly-module-federation would need a test-utils package, which\nis not worth introducing here. RecordingLogger.ts is already duplicated\nacross the two the same way.\n\ncore 142/142, firefly-module-federation 117/117, lint and tsgo clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: one recorder instead of two near-identical ones\n\nRecordingLogger and ScopeRecordingLogger were line-for-line identical\napart from where a scope parks its output: same #segments buffering, same\n#write, same five level methods, same four no-op with* chainers. Two\nrecorders in one folder drift the moment LoggerScope or RootLogger gains\na member — the same argument the DummyRuntime commit makes here.\n\nScopeRecordingLogger is the strictly stronger view, so it grew a flat\n\"logs\" getter and RecordingLogger is gone from both packages. Net -284\nlines.\n\nThe getter is documented as order-approximate, which is the one real\ndifference: the shipped logger shares a single list between the root and\nits scopes, so root and scope logs interleave there and not in the\nderived view. Every assertion against it is a toContain or a count, so\nnone depends on that. The comment says to assert on \"scopes\" instead if\nan order-sensitive assertion is ever wanted.\n\nMutation-checked again after the swap, because replacing a test double is\nexactly how tests go quietly vacuous: with the success log moved back\nbelow the try/catch, the example suite still fails.\n\ncore 142/142, firefly-module-federation 117/117, lint and tsgo clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb72eb62b5f15511c0469acb8aecf75389383934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/cb72eb62b5f15511c0469acb8aecf75389383934"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/b8bfd7caf4286c5cffbf449d2ea211ae49c5b8dc","verification":{"payload":"tree cb72eb62b5f15511c0469acb8aecf75389383934\nparent 3397f6eadcac3fb2da554e397324dff04e4a0176\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787774165 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787774165 -0400\n\nfix(core): stop reporting a failed registration as successful (#682)\n\n* fix(core): stop reporting a failed registration as successful\n\nThe \"Successfully registered/updated ...\" log sat after the try/catch in\nfive of the six module registration paths, so it also ran on the error\npath: the failure was logged, the scope was ended red, a\nModuleRegistrationError was pushed, and then the success log was written\nand the scope ended a second time.\n\nBoth loggers that implement a logger scope today, @workleap/logging and\n@workleap/logrocket, buffer a scope''s logs and flush them from end(), and\nboth ignore a second end() call, so the stray log was queued into an\nalready ended scope and discarded. The defect is invisible with every\nlogger that currently exists and surfaces only for one that writes each\nlog as it is called. Verified against both dists rather than assumed.\n\nThe success log and its end() move inside the try, which is the shape\nRemoteModuleRegistry.registerModules already used. That site was already\ncorrect and is left untouched.\n\nThe tests record through a write-through logger that also records scope\nends as \"end:<color>\". The moved end() is half the fix, and asserting on\nlog text alone does not observe it: deleting every green end() left the\nwhole suite passing. All six sites are now covered, including the\nreference one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: pin the registration logging invariants across every failure mask\n\nThe cherry-picked fix ships example-based tests: one failing module next\nto one succeeding one, per loop. That pins the defect that was found. It\ndoes not pin the property, so the next rearrangement of these loops has\none example standing between it and a silent regression.\n\nThese assert the structure instead. For each of the 6 registration loops,\nall 16 combinations of which of 4 modules fail, reduced to one comparison:\n\n- a success line appears exactly as many times as the loop counted a\n  completion\n- every scope ends exactly once\n- no scope reports both outcomes, or neither\n- the colour of a scope''s end agrees with its outcome\n\nAttribution per scope is what the flat RecordingLogger cannot give. The\ntotals alone pass a mask with as many successes as failures while a\nsuccess line sits in a scope that failed, which is precisely the defect.\n\nMutation-verified, since none of this is worth anything if it cannot fail:\n\n- success log moved back below the try/catch — kills 15/16 masks; the\n  survivor is \"no module fails\", which takes no error path\n- green end() deleted — kills 15/16; the survivor is \"every module\n  fails\", where every scope already ends red exactly once so a missing\n  green end is unobservable\n- same move applied to RemoteModuleRegistry.registerModules, the site\n  that was already correct and that the other five were changed to match\n  — kills 15/16, so that coverage is not vacuous\n\nThe two local mutations are complementary: every mask is killed by at\nleast one. Mutations were run in a separate worktree, not here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(changeset): stop the first sentence reading as an output change\n\n\"reporting a failed registration as successfully registered\" describes\nthe code accurately but reads, on its own, as though a console line\nchanged. Nothing a consumer sees changed, and the second paragraph\nalready says so — the first sentence should not undo it.\n\nReworded to describe the code path rather than an outcome.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: share DummyRuntime instead of copying it per test file\n\nDummyRuntime was defined inline in four test files, byte-identical in all\nfour (868 bytes each). Two copies per package drift the moment Runtime\ngains an abstract member, and the compiler only reports whichever file it\ncompiles first.\n\nExtracted to packages/core/tests/DummyRuntime.ts and to the module\nfederation package''s existing tests/utils.ts, and imported from both test\nfiles in each package. Net -123 lines.\n\nThe cross-package half is left alone: sharing between @squide/core and\n@squide/firefly-module-federation would need a test-utils package, which\nis not worth introducing here. RecordingLogger.ts is already duplicated\nacross the two the same way.\n\ncore 142/142, firefly-module-federation 117/117, lint and tsgo clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: one recorder instead of two near-identical ones\n\nRecordingLogger and ScopeRecordingLogger were line-for-line identical\napart from where a scope parks its output: same #segments buffering, same\n#write, same five level methods, same four no-op with* chainers. Two\nrecorders in one folder drift the moment LoggerScope or RootLogger gains\na member — the same argument the DummyRuntime commit makes here.\n\nScopeRecordingLogger is the strictly stronger view, so it grew a flat\n\"logs\" getter and RecordingLogger is gone from both packages. Net -284\nlines.\n\nThe getter is documented as order-approximate, which is the one real\ndifference: the shipped logger shares a single list between the root and\nits scopes, so root and scope logs interleave there and not in the\nderived view. Every assertion against it is a toContain or a count, so\nnone depends on that. The comment says to assert on \"scopes\" instead if\nan order-sensitive assertion is ever wanted.\n\nMutation-checked again after the swap, because replacing a test double is\nexactly how tests go quietly vacuous: with the success log moved back\nbelow the try/catch, the example suite still fails.\n\ncore 142/142, firefly-module-federation 117/117, lint and tsgo clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj0TVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS9oQAHyYvqCdyS9EQTJgaT+4ocmX\nA0Q0pv3Vxx4td8ztmuan5yakTusLQqEs2krXDznzBZ3PIm68Fz7fig5OW7N4mYz3\nEBS5F7uxBW4HIij6mF7t/GLLuCF00UNAgjk/Q72QyDT26dwf92xrhmcVVI8RANVW\nZR/9qCRKaKxq6hxdzvKwPl/zTiTVJSVRzfI5FIxQLAkthl3yetcfzyv2Gdd9tvWf\nk6hHFMhQr3LXZUagx9gD7IdjE/u+gV40BW7iWOMlAixc