,"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/3397f6eadcac3fb2da554e397324dff04e4a0176","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKDMzOTdmNmVhZGNhYzNmYjJkYTU1NGUzOTczMjRkZmYwNGU0YTAxNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/4d65ac00c3094d9276c7c9f5914499863701032b","sha":"4d65ac00c3094d9276c7c9f5914499863701032b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/4d65ac00c3094d9276c7c9f5914499863701032b"}],"sha":"3397f6eadcac3fb2da554e397324dff04e4a0176","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/3397f6eadcac3fb2da554e397324dff04e4a0176"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/4d65ac00c3094d9276c7c9f5914499863701032b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:38:18Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:38:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"revert: registration reporting and navigation item correctness (#671) (#678)\n\n* revert: registration reporting and navigation item correctness (#671)\n\nReverts fb2669e985e20d71363d50d6d703033afaf1c7a9, returning the source of\npackages/ to the state it had at 23c6bfb6a (@squide/firefly@18.3.0,\n@squide/react-router@9.2.0, @squide/core@7.1.1).\n\nThat commit bundled three fixes in a single change. One of them introduced\ndefects in the navigation item registry that were not caught before release,\nand because the three were entangled in the same commit the whole bundle comes\nout rather than a piece of it. The three changesets it carried are withdrawn:\nbrave-moons-argue, tidy-pandas-repeat and witty-carrots-jam.\n\nThe release commit dc543e493 is deliberately NOT reverted. Its CHANGELOG\nentries and package.json version bumps are the public record of what was\npublished, and npm versions are immutable, so the rollback moves forward to a\nnew version containing the old code rather than back to an existing one.\n\nVerified: git diff 23c6bfb6a -- packages/ shows only CHANGELOG.md and\npackage.json version lines, with no src/ or tests/ difference at all.\n\nAlso removes three claims from agent-skills/ that 6fa503548 derived from the\nreverted docs and that the revert makes false: that Squide clones registered\nsections, and (in components.md and patterns.md) that navigation items are\nre-validated after every deferred registration update. Verified against the\nreverted source: NavigationItemRegistry does no cloning, and\nuseStrictRegistrationMode validates only once, when the modules become ready.\nThe rest of 6fa503548 is unrelated and is left in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address code-review findings on the revert\n\nTwo findings from the code-review job on #678.\n\n1. agent-skills/.../patterns.md stated that Squide \"copies\" the navigation\n   sections registered by a deferred registration function, so mutating a\n   section after registering it does not change what the menu renders. The\n   revert makes that false: NavigationItemRegistry.#addNestedItem assigns\n   straight onto the module''s own object\n   (parentSection.item.children = [...]), with no copy anywhere in the class.\n   The equivalent claim was already removed from SKILL.md and from\n   docs/essentials/register-deferred-nav-items.md; this copy was missed\n   because it says \"copies\" rather than \"clones\".\n\n2. Restored the strictMode documentation on AppRouter, without the\n   re-validation claims the revert invalidates.\n\n   The finding framed this as the revert over-reaching, which is not quite\n   right — strictMode was documented nowhere at 23c6bfb6a, so removing it\n   was faithful and the gap is pre-existing. But the prop is real and\n   shipped (AppRouter.tsx:92, default true), and the surgical skill edit\n   kept it documented, so docs/ and the skill contradicted each other.\n   Documenting it in both is the better end state.\n\n   Dropped from the restored text: \"validates the navigation item\n   registrations again after every deferred registration update\" and the\n   paragraph about routes being frozen and validated only once, which\n   described the removed includeRoutes distinction. Post-revert everything\n   validates once, when the modules become ready.\n\n   Verified against the reverted source: strictMode defaults to true,\n   useStrictRegistrationMode validates when the modules are ready, and\n   RootRoute passes throwWhenThereIsNoMatch: strictMode.\n\nAlso widened the stale-claim sweep beyond the literal word \"clone\" to cover\ncopy/clone semantics, ownership and mutation claims, re-validation claims and\nthe removed API surface across agent-skills/ and docs/. No further hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address second round of bot review findings\n\nFour accepted findings, all documentation. No source change, so the green\nbuild/test/typecheck run on 0a77207c still holds.\n\n- docs/essentials/register-deferred-nav-items.md: restored the two sections\n  the revert deleted wholesale. Only the \"Squide copies the navigation\n  sections\" warning described reverted behaviour; the clear-then-replay\n  \"register the full set\" contract predates #671 (clearDeferredItems is\n  untouched) and the missing-section report still fires once the modules are\n  ready. The skill''s patterns.md kept both, and sync-agent-skill drives the\n  skill from docs/, so leaving docs/ empty would have let the next sync strip\n  accurate guidance.\n\n- agent-skills/.../patterns.md: the missing-section paragraph still advertised\n  catching \"a deferred registration function that stops registering a section\"\n  — the one scenario the revert stops reporting. Rewritten to scope the\n  guarantee to bootstrap and state the update-run gap outright.\n\n- agent-skills/.../components.md: \"Routes are only validated once\" was a\n  contrast with navigation items being re-validated per update run. Post-revert\n  both validate exactly once, so the wording implied the reverted behaviour.\n\n- agent-skills/.../SKILL.md: bumped metadata.version 1.16 -> 1.17, required by\n  agent-docs/references/agent-skills.md for any edit under agent-skills/.\n\nDeclined: restoring ADR-0022/0023 as deprecated rather than deleting them.\nBoth were status \"proposed\" (awaiting human review, never accepted), so the\nREADME''s \"supersede a prior decision, do not silently ignore it\" rule does not\napply — there was no accepted decision. No tracked file and no published\nCHANGELOG references either number; only git history does, which points at a\ndeleted file whether or not the number is reused.\n\nDeclined as out of scope: two findings on restored pre-existing code — the\n\"navigation item(s)\" wording in the strict-mode report and the tests asserting\non the literal section index key. packages/ is byte-identical to 23c6bfb6a, so\nboth predate #671. The index key is tracked to re-land on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address third round of bot review findings\n\nBoth accepted, both documentation. No source change.\n\n- agent-docs/adr/0006-pending-registration-queue.md: the revert restored a\n  line reference that lands 16 lines off. #pendingRegistrationsIndex is at\n  NavigationItemRegistry.ts:167; lines 151-153 are the tail of the\n  parseSectionIndexKey deprecation JSDoc. The reference was already stale at\n  23c6bfb6a, which is why fb2669e98 replaced it with a by-name reference —\n  that part is format-independent and survives the revert. Replaced only the\n  NavigationItemRegistry reference; the RouteRegistry line numbers in the same\n  sentence were verified accurate (#pendingRegistrationsIndex at 120,\n  #tryRegisterPendingRoutes at 179) and are left alone. CLAUDE.md sends agents\n  to this ADR before touching the registries, so the pointer has to land.\n\n- .changeset/revert-671.md: documented that parseSectionIndexKey reverts to\n  indexKey.split(\"-\"). It is public API — packages/react-router/src/index.ts\n  re-exports the module and packages/firefly/src/index.ts re-exports that — so\n  a caller on 18.4.0 loses the guaranteed two-element result. The changeset is\n  otherwise exhaustive about what an 18.4.0 adopter loses, and this was the one\n  silent behaviour change missing from it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9762c3142baf403d6e537b49806107b6024a1415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/9762c3142baf403d6e537b49806107b6024a1415"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/4d65ac00c3094d9276c7c9f5914499863701032b","verification":{"payload":"tree 9762c3142baf403d6e537b49806107b6024a1415\nparent 6fa503548fce96f05fb77b2170aa02b839a1df21\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787755098 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787755098 -0400\n\nrevert: registration reporting and navigation item correctness (#671) (#678)\n\n* revert: registration reporting and navigation item correctness (#671)\n\nReverts fb2669e985e20d71363d50d6d703033afaf1c7a9, returning the source of\npackages/ to the state it had at 23c6bfb6a (@squide/firefly@18.3.0,\n@squide/react-router@9.2.0, @squide/core@7.1.1).\n\nThat commit bundled three fixes in a single change. One of them introduced\ndefects in the navigation item registry that were not caught before release,\nand because the three were entangled in the same commit the whole bundle comes\nout rather than a piece of it. The three changesets it carried are withdrawn:\nbrave-moons-argue, tidy-pandas-repeat and witty-carrots-jam.\n\nThe release commit dc543e493 is deliberately NOT reverted. Its CHANGELOG\nentries and package.json version bumps are the public record of what was\npublished, and npm versions are immutable, so the rollback moves forward to a\nnew version containing the old code rather than back to an existing one.\n\nVerified: git diff 23c6bfb6a -- packages/ shows only CHANGELOG.md and\npackage.json version lines, with no src/ or tests/ difference at all.\n\nAlso removes three claims from agent-skills/ that 6fa503548 derived from the\nreverted docs and that the revert makes false: that Squide clones registered\nsections, and (in components.md and patterns.md) that navigation items are\nre-validated after every deferred registration update. Verified against the\nreverted source: NavigationItemRegistry does no cloning, and\nuseStrictRegistrationMode validates only once, when the modules become ready.\nThe rest of 6fa503548 is unrelated and is left in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address code-review findings on the revert\n\nTwo findings from the code-review job on #678.\n\n1. agent-skills/.../patterns.md stated that Squide \"copies\" the navigation\n   sections registered by a deferred registration function, so mutating a\n   section after registering it does not change what the menu renders. The\n   revert makes that false: NavigationItemRegistry.#addNestedItem assigns\n   straight onto the module''s own object\n   (parentSection.item.children = [...]), with no copy anywhere in the class.\n   The equivalent claim was already removed from SKILL.md and from\n   docs/essentials/register-deferred-nav-items.md; this copy was missed\n   because it says \"copies\" rather than \"clones\".\n\n2. Restored the strictMode documentation on AppRouter, without the\n   re-validation claims the revert invalidates.\n\n   The finding framed this as the revert over-reaching, which is not quite\n   right — strictMode was documented nowhere at 23c6bfb6a, so removing it\n   was faithful and the gap is pre-existing. But the prop is real and\n   shipped (AppRouter.tsx:92, default true), and the surgical skill edit\n   kept it documented, so docs/ and the skill contradicted each other.\n   Documenting it in both is the better end state.\n\n   Dropped from the restored text: \"validates the navigation item\n   registrations again after every deferred registration update\" and the\n   paragraph about routes being frozen and validated only once, which\n   described the removed includeRoutes distinction. Post-revert everything\n   validates once, when the modules become ready.\n\n   Verified against the reverted source: strictMode defaults to true,\n   useStrictRegistrationMode validates when the modules are ready, and\n   RootRoute passes throwWhenThereIsNoMatch: strictMode.\n\nAlso widened the stale-claim sweep beyond the literal word \"clone\" to cover\ncopy/clone semantics, ownership and mutation claims, re-validation claims and\nthe removed API surface across agent-skills/ and docs/. No further hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address second round of bot review findings\n\nFour accepted findings, all documentation. No source change, so the green\nbuild/test/typecheck run on 0a77207c still holds.\n\n- docs/essentials/register-deferred-nav-items.md: restored the two sections\n  the revert deleted wholesale. Only the \"Squide copies the navigation\n  sections\" warning described reverted behaviour; the clear-then-replay\n  \"register the full set\" contract predates #671 (clearDeferredItems is\n  untouched) and the missing-section report still fires once the modules are\n  ready. The skill''s patterns.md kept both, and sync-agent-skill drives the\n  skill from docs/, so leaving docs/ empty would have let the next sync strip\n  accurate guidance.\n\n- agent-skills/.../patterns.md: the missing-section paragraph still advertised\n  catching \"a deferred registration function that stops registering a section\"\n  — the one scenario the revert stops reporting. Rewritten to scope the\n  guarantee to bootstrap and state the update-run gap outright.\n\n- agent-skills/.../components.md: \"Routes are only validated once\" was a\n  contrast with navigation items being re-validated per update run. Post-revert\n  both validate exactly once, so the wording implied the reverted behaviour.\n\n- agent-skills/.../SKILL.md: bumped metadata.version 1.16 -> 1.17, required by\n  agent-docs/references/agent-skills.md for any edit under agent-skills/.\n\nDeclined: restoring ADR-0022/0023 as deprecated rather than deleting them.\nBoth were status \"proposed\" (awaiting human review, never accepted), so the\nREADME''s \"supersede a prior decision, do not silently ignore it\" rule does not\napply — there was no accepted decision. No tracked file and no published\nCHANGELOG references either number; only git history does, which points at a\ndeleted file whether or not the number is reused.\n\nDeclined as out of scope: two findings on restored pre-existing code — the\n\"navigation item(s)\" wording in the strict-mode report and the tests asserting\non the literal section index key. packages/ is byte-identical to 23c6bfb6a, so\nboth predate #671. The index key is tracked to re-land on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address third round of bot review findings\n\nBoth accepted, both documentation. No source change.\n\n- agent-docs/adr/0006-pending-registration-queue.md: the revert restored a\n  line reference that lands 16 lines off. #pendingRegistrationsIndex is at\n  NavigationItemRegistry.ts:167; lines 151-153 are the tail of the\n  parseSectionIndexKey deprecation JSDoc. The reference was already stale at\n  23c6bfb6a, which is why fb2669e98 replaced it with a by-name reference —\n  that part is format-independent and survives the revert. Replaced only the\n  NavigationItemRegistry reference; the RouteRegistry line numbers in the same\n  sentence were verified accurate (#pendingRegistrationsIndex at 120,\n  #tryRegisterPendingRoutes at 179) and are left alone. CLAUDE.md sends agents\n  to this ADR before touching the registries, so the pointer has to land.\n\n- .changeset/revert-671.md: documented that parseSectionIndexKey reverts to\n  indexKey.split(\"-\"). It is public API — packages/react-router/src/index.ts\n  re-exports the module and packages/firefly/src/index.ts re-exports that — so\n  a caller on 18.4.0 loses the guaranteed two-element result. The changeset is\n  otherwise exhaustive about what an 18.4.0 adopter loses, and this was the one\n  silent behaviour change missing from it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"va