reply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(changesets): version packages (#668)\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"27975f0c0aa2e8e9216b0d02395712c193b9d3ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/27975f0c0aa2e8e9216b0d02395712c193b9d3ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/23c6bfb6a14f109369b882d6dea24b7db19a7c05","verification":{"payload":"tree 27975f0c0aa2e8e9216b0d02395712c193b9d3ef\nparent aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787606191 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787606191 -0400\n\nci(changesets): version packages (#668)\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjLSvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQkUQAKzOy/QefR07rIwOzfNjHcWX\nTQhhhldf9TpD4OeS23AKV3aboXrRmYpnXJf3hGmXgybiYJDbWSxs+KZrYm+b4rY/\nZNofKnfP9D8uYcVbl459gv5ciaKI3uCFyotQwl1afaZNSIqoh3i4BsdiqZk4aCwB\ntHIp4sM+VibWlWlPrs0SsZWg7LrkF8sowQ1fmnKvNmfQOC1gm77wX9rTIccDtgco\nHsBx9OsITD0GrspTR76zKUbxEs/2EzVGHcVXAr26MLfoXB6OoYwK+CR9TGPFLl5Q\nbHFNqE9M5KAMawgVy94kHdM1sVi3qINdAXs+jcZJfGZXlKZy/Ub0U8EwYBVk7lIz\n/3bspjY8esJe3rbYMN++lpE/PtkY0D8tnAj6YsSAzjk0PsVcl1/yWZhJB34+Gucq\n+dI3Eqp9+ObGZ66uC8zLt0R0LoG9eQQK9nIc+URWuny2621hHYeIV7lSGmbDluo5\nN9sEQDJiQBXCTf9HIgtG+WplJ7i09/SZqUdXe4uPalMtcExja2DHlAsgtltUcwEj\n4Ts9t5yzD2D09/5eXl9zuB8JQsxXYoNhf7USdtgRwsNVVsEi+5eeR+jTazzDAPPi\nvovLROP1xNPfjvmzRAIBG5aLfBP1J3ai1/mxgbWZ6+rzoI+rxnbv2M7z2Lfxj4LT\n0zD67EAlZrrYOsuDJz30\n=O+6Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T21:16:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/23c6bfb6a14f109369b882d6dea24b7db19a7c05","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKDIzYzZiZmI2YTE0ZjEwOTM2OWI4ODJkNmRlYTI0YjdkYjE5YTdjMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd","sha":"aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd"}],"sha":"23c6bfb6a14f109369b882d6dea24b7db19a7c05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/23c6bfb6a14f109369b882d6dea24b7db19a7c05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:53:51Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:53:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(react-router): deferred registrations update run registry corruption (#667)\n\n* fix(react-router): deferred registrations update run registry corruption\n\nThree defects on the transactional (update) deferred registration path, plus\nthe scope leak that made them undiagnosable. Reported in #658.\n\n- clearDeferredItems() never purged #pendingRegistrationsIndex, so a deferred\n  nested item whose section was missing survived every clear and was replayed\n  in addition to the item registered by the current run. Toggling a feature\n  flag off and on duplicated every nested item of the gated section.\n- #deleteDeferredSectionIndexEntries scanned the whole section index but\n  deleted against the current menu''s key namespace, so a static section\n  sharing an $id with another menu''s deferred section lost its index entry on\n  the first update run. It is now a single pass deleting by the actual map\n  key, which also collects entries orphaned by a failed registration.\n- completeDeferredRegistrationScope released the active scope only when\n  complete() returned normally, so a throw bricked every subsequent update for\n  the lifetime of the runtime. The error is still propagated.\n- Navigation item validation messages parsed the menu id and section id back\n  out of the index key by splitting on \"-\", which is lossy. They are now read\n  off the pending items, which carry both. parseSectionIndexKey is deprecated\n  and PendingRegistrationItem is exported.\n\nThe comment justifying the hardcoded \"registered\" status is corrected rather\nthan removed: the status is still inaccurate on the update path, which is\ntracked separately.\n\nRegression tests drive a real update run end to end through\ncreateDeferredRegistrationsRunner, which the issue identified as the coverage\ngap that let all of this through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(react-router): address review feedback on the update run fixes\n\n- The three changesets now list @squide/firefly. It re-exports\n  @squide/react-router, so PendingRegistrationItem becomes a new public export\n  there and parseSectionIndexKey a deprecation, which the internal dependency\n  bump alone would have shipped as a patch.\n- The orphaned section index entry bullet says \"deferred\". Only deferred\n  orphans are cleared, a static one still throws for the lifetime of the\n  runtime, which is correct since clearDeferredItems does not own static state.\n- The parseSectionIndexKey deprecation no longer redirects to\n  getPendingRegistrationsForSection. The navigation item registry is protected\n  on the runtime with no public accessor, so no consumer can obtain an index\n  key to parse in the first place. The function is kept only to avoid a\n  breaking removal, and the note now says what the hazard actually is: the key\n  is ambiguous, not merely unparseable.\n- Validation no longer destructures pendingItems[0] unguarded. A key in the\n  index always holds at least one item, but getPendingRegistrationsForSection\n  hands out the live internal array, so a caller can empty it and turn the\n  diagnostic into a TypeError that masks the registrations it was reporting.\n- Added a regression test pinning the registration type guard. Purging only the\n  deferred pending registrations relies on it to keep a static section from\n  accumulating deferred children across a clear, and nothing covered it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(react-router): correct the parseSectionIndexKey deprecation rationale\n\nRaised in review of #667.\n\nThe note claimed no public API hands out section index keys. It does:\nNavigationItemRegistry is exported from the package and its\ngetPendingRegistrations().getPendingSectionIds() returns exactly those keys, so\na consumer holding one had parseSectionIndexKey as their only way to read it.\nDeprecating on that rationale would have removed the function in the next major\nand left them without a migration path.\n\nThe note and the changeset now justify the deprecation on the ambiguity alone\nand point at PendingRegistrationItem, whose \"menuId\" and \"sectionId\" are\nreachable from the same object that hands out the key.\n\nAlso renamed a deferred registrations runner test. Its title claimed the nested\nitem registration is not left pending, which the test neither asserts nor\nachieves, since the replay re-registers an item whose section is still missing.\nWhat it verifies is that those registrations do not accumulate across runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"087684297fd6929e029988f0476e33ac5d2fc936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/087684297fd6929e029988f0476e33ac5d2fc936"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd","verification":{"payload":"tree 087684297fd6929e029988f0476e33ac5d2fc936\nparent fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787604831 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787604831 -0400\n\nfix(react-router): deferred registrations update run registry corruption (#667)\n\n* fix(react-router): deferred registrations update run registry corruption\n\nThree defects on the transactional (update) deferred registration path, plus\nthe scope leak that made them undiagnosable. Reported in #658.\n\n- clearDeferredItems() never purged #pendingRegistrationsIndex, so a deferred\n  nested item whose section was missing survived every clear and was replayed\n  in addition to the item registered by the current run. Toggling a feature\n  flag off and on duplicated every nested item of the gated section.\n- #deleteDeferredSectionIndexEntries scanned the whole section index but\n  deleted against the current menu''s key namespace, so a static section\n  sharing an $id with another menu''s deferred section lost its index entry on\n  the first update run. It is now a single pass deleting by the actual map\n  key, which also collects entries orphaned by a failed registration.\n- completeDeferredRegistrationScope released the active scope only when\n  complete() returned normally, so a throw bricked every subsequent update for\n  the lifetime of the runtime. The error is still propagated.\n- Navigation item validation messages parsed the menu id and section id back\n  out of the index key by splitting on \"-\", which is lossy. They are now read\n  off the pending items, which carry both. parseSectionIndexKey is deprecated\n  and PendingRegistrationItem is exported.\n\nThe comment justifying the hardcoded \"registered\" status is corrected rather\nthan removed: the status is still inaccurate on the update path, which is\ntracked separately.\n\nRegression tests drive a real update run end to end through\ncreateDeferredRegistrationsRunner, which the issue identified as the coverage\ngap that let all of this through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(react-router): address review feedback on the update run fixes\n\n- The three changesets now list @squide/firefly. It re-exports\n  @squide/react-router, so PendingRegistrationItem becomes a new public export\n  there and parseSectionIndexKey a deprecation, which the internal dependency\n  bump alone would have shipped as a patch.\n- The orphaned section index entry bullet says \"deferred\". Only deferred\n  orphans are cleared, a static one still throws for the lifetime of the\n  runtime, which is correct since clearDeferredItems does not own static state.\n- The parseSectionIndexKey deprecation no longer redirects to\n  getPendingRegistrationsForSection. The navigation item registry is protected\n  on the runtime with no public accessor, so no consumer can obtain an index\n  key to parse in the first place. The function is kept only to avoid a\n  breaking removal, and the note now says what the hazard actually is: the key\n  is ambiguous, not merely unparseable.\n- Validation no longer destructures pendingItems[0] unguarded. A key in the\n  index always holds at least one item, but getPendingRegistrationsForSection\n  hands out the live internal array, so a caller can empty it and turn the\n  diagnostic into a TypeError that masks the registrations it was reporting.\n- Added a regression test pinning the registration type guard. Purging only the\n  deferred pending registrations relies on it to keep a static section from\n  accumulating deferred children across a clear, and nothing covered it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(react-router): correct the parseSectionIndexKey deprecation rationale\n\nRaised in review of #667.\n\nThe note claimed no public API hands out section index keys. It does:\nNavigationItemRegistry is exported from the package and its\ngetPendingRegistrations().getPendingSectionIds() returns exactly those keys, so\na consumer holding one had parseSectionIndexKey as their only way to read it.\nDeprecating on that rationale would have removed the function in the next major\nand left them without a migration path.\n\nThe note and the changeset now justify the deprecation on the ambiguity alone\nand point at PendingRegistrationItem, whose \"menuId\" and \"sectionId\" are\nreachable from the same object that hands out the key.\n\nAlso renamed a deferred registrations runner test. Its title claimed the nested\nitem registration is not left pending, which the test neither asserts nor\nachieves, since the replay re-registers an item whose section is still missing.\nWhat it verifies is that those registrations do not accumulate across runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjK9fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACrgQAFNyAWJxbJ+JCtQo8pjCTKeF\nouh16YjM+t6ChDj/BzOHMG1UZvr64OK+JHeor/3GGZJX6rVh+gSJC84kEn3ykFHD\ntfE2AvZjY3VpWDENhUa0zrlBi6fXElr2wBWt7tpK01LO9O6SKVVkfCfwYfHMh6+4\n4s8oYZBqtSMR8bxaO5c8CcvltUu6LN+1Ef37jEgPN2q06BYoGPNh1TQUTLgoTVmR\nomvt+HpOc2WFe4eWCvtkthckVJsyP660yzzysN9PKO7jhZ+UlxK48xNhUqn3OIhx\niDGxmF+/mv/MXr26T8rUsPMrimouObZ+FdatJgTdWdrSoxD0/eFcSz5slZgOfbHr\nv6nUCHeQP5FJ9cQhVRBr/tRv9WZDLr2GX+zLolnv2wc06BGHBRvRPNkh4r6zF6zT\n+OFVkZ0n6UmhiEF1p/HQIfzVF1qIU+SKEoZbiNowrptYyEhwaepVlL7VHDkYYaek\niSQlCTBQbs8nBJtceIWCDSidxoeLlerDQaqAxXuolJsQb9qENrePuh/xOimQZBPH\ngvs9zzp+h0kUGA0ETNF0rsOtQkxFET6Rj22y7j+xawDoWcsN7N169+NvbrLUbTQ+\niVwIpqAh+hJzbiOkMJEP4wEA0LC7rAJtKMr0Mvxoh0rAjtRcL3jqcRK0+FlQpFeA\nC631z080AzTDZDmmLaj2\n=Sr/u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T20:53:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKGFhYjQ1MmMxZmRmNDA3OTljZmVkY2I3Mjk1NmEzMmNkZjYwYzQ1Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0","sha":"fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0"}],"sha":"aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/aab452c1fdf40799cfedcb72956a32cdf60c45cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://a