UD36XUvCuOGjnVOJMi923mAkLWoQammcWfKDE9MKZcltTQ0diX3UruzcJ1eV\nr8OrQCNCiPpmeYrAfJj/Wxrjqhx/YvSEIOJ/yA0RvwvkaomjzgDIK9p0y+4VUuOW\neZYcSrm18FdnG/kYHdCdUJ+QWiZo213oTYQRDb6/OF7P1Gt/nOQ2iMPE2N9sj0C/\n+ZBjDcsvXIovyR6p75uQzgCBQj6o3Uk+BAtecTpZBDnoycBoAw4DCaQq8hQjmWRr\nqYPN+1Xxr+mzLJbmXocn\n=6vjQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T19:05:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0","node_id":"C_kwDOJbZi_NoAKGZhOTZkZDg2YjUxNjAxOTYzZmM3MzU2N2I0ODVmNWFhMGEwZmE1ZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/workleap/wl-squide/commit/7925636fb6c2c448279dca87262c7f72bd9500cb","sha":"7925636fb6c2c448279dca87262c7f72bd9500cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/7925636fb6c2c448279dca87262c7f72bd9500cb"}],"sha":"fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/fa96dd86b51601963fc73567b485f5aa0a0fa5e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/7925636fb6c2c448279dca87262c7f72bd9500cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T19:03:01Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T19:03:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(react-router): add a $meta channel to navigation items (#665)\n\n* feat(react-router): add a $meta channel to navigation items\n\n$additionalProps served two incompatible purposes: the reference docs\ndescribed it as a forwarding channel while the essentials guide used it\nas a metadata bag that the renderer had to strip before spreading. The\nsplit was per-key and implicit, so a module could add a key and a\nrenderer written elsewhere would silently emit it as a DOM attribute.\n\nNavigation items now carry both $additionalProps, spread onto the\nrendered component, and $meta, read by the renderer and never spread.\nBoth surface on the render props, defaulting to {} so renderers can\ndestructure unconditionally. Purely additive.\n\ntoLinkProps also strips every $ prefixed key generically instead of\nomitting a fixed list. The previous named-omit plus rest-spread leaked\nany unlisted $ property onto the DOM, so adding $meta without touching\nit would have reproduced the bug this fixes. It also drops a nested\nitem $priority, which leaked before.\n\nCloses #661\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(react-router): keep the existing toLinkProps style, drop ADR-0022\n\nFiltering the rest element gives the same result as filtering the whole\nitem, so toLinkProps keeps its signature destructuring instead of taking\nthe item and destructuring in the body. stripMetadataProps is generic,\nwhich also removes the cast at the call site: the rest type stays the one\nTypeScript inferred rather than one asserted back onto it.\n\n$id no longer needs naming, since it was only listed to exclude it, so\nthe eslint-disable and its typo comment go away too.\n\nADR-0022 removed along with the index rows referencing it. ADR-0018 keeps\nthree corrections its own text now needs: $meta in the property list and\nthe evidence line, and the \"must be kept in sync\" consequence, which the\ngeneric filter makes false.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add an $additionalProps usage example to useRenderedNavigationItems\n\nThe page documented the option in its type lists but only showed $meta\nbeing used. The new section mirrors the \"Read item metadata\" one and\nreuses the \"about\" item with a \"data-tracking-id\" prop, matching the\nexamples in the essentials guide and the FireflyRuntime reference.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback\n\n- Cover the nested case in the strip test. The claim that the generic\n  filter fixes a nested \"$priority\" leak was untested, since all five\n  new tests registered root level items only.\n- Update both MessagePage samples, which still told the reader the\n  navbar highlight came from custom additional props.\n- Add \"meta\" to the render props table in the skill''s hooks reference.\n  The table arrived from main via #664 and is the authoritative property\n  list an agent reads, so omitting \"meta\" contradicted the example below\n  it.\n- Fix a sentence fragment in the essentials warning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79e68ab5ece8a8c145bee9b93ef3c907e0ebccba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/79e68ab5ece8a8c145bee9b93ef3c907e0ebccba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/7925636fb6c2c448279dca87262c7f72bd9500cb","verification":{"payload":"tree 79e68ab5ece8a8c145bee9b93ef3c907e0ebccba\nparent 4e854187407f13e0e5faaee35098324a976b728e\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787598181 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787598181 -0400\n\nfeat(react-router): add a $meta channel to navigation items (#665)\n\n* feat(react-router): add a $meta channel to navigation items\n\n$additionalProps served two incompatible purposes: the reference docs\ndescribed it as a forwarding channel while the essentials guide used it\nas a metadata bag that the renderer had to strip before spreading. The\nsplit was per-key and implicit, so a module could add a key and a\nrenderer written elsewhere would silently emit it as a DOM attribute.\n\nNavigation items now carry both $additionalProps, spread onto the\nrendered component, and $meta, read by the renderer and never spread.\nBoth surface on the render props, defaulting to {} so renderers can\ndestructure unconditionally. Purely additive.\n\ntoLinkProps also strips every $ prefixed key generically instead of\nomitting a fixed list. The previous named-omit plus rest-spread leaked\nany unlisted $ property onto the DOM, so adding $meta without touching\nit would have reproduced the bug this fixes. It also drops a nested\nitem $priority, which leaked before.\n\nCloses #661\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(react-router): keep the existing toLinkProps style, drop ADR-0022\n\nFiltering the rest element gives the same result as filtering the whole\nitem, so toLinkProps keeps its signature destructuring instead of taking\nthe item and destructuring in the body. stripMetadataProps is generic,\nwhich also removes the cast at the call site: the rest type stays the one\nTypeScript inferred rather than one asserted back onto it.\n\n$id no longer needs naming, since it was only listed to exclude it, so\nthe eslint-disable and its typo comment go away too.\n\nADR-0022 removed along with the index rows referencing it. ADR-0018 keeps\nthree corrections its own text now needs: $meta in the property list and\nthe evidence line, and the \"must be kept in sync\" consequence, which the\ngeneric filter makes false.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add an $additionalProps usage example to useRenderedNavigationItems\n\nThe page documented the option in its type lists but only showed $meta\nbeing used. The new section mirrors the \"Read item metadata\" one and\nreuses the \"about\" item with a \"data-tracking-id\" prop, matching the\nexamples in the essentials guide and the FireflyRuntime reference.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback\n\n- Cover the nested case in the strip test. The claim that the generic\n  filter fixes a nested \"$priority\" leak was untested, since all five\n  new tests registered root level items only.\n- Update both MessagePage samples, which still told the reader the\n  navbar highlight came from custom additional props.\n- Add \"meta\" to the render props table in the skill''s hooks reference.\n  The table arrived from main via #664 and is the authoritative property\n  list an agent reads, so omitting \"meta\" contradicted the example below\n  it.\n- Fix a sentence fragment in the essentials warning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjJVlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEEEQAIin23/8tD4k7oTlWOUzaRS7\n87Npfn1d3LfENqd43/rwco4YW+C36ZYEW0+nvDxEU/+E4HNjZy8M9xVvtWvru3+e\n+IWJeFMKPg88FK0SKSwGQqmdCBc+BkD0gJXCjPmKTHDbIYNsHEEwPIbDN+VTjN/p\nOFPtPs3YAt7lSMatJQmaMsus79QHQULLZk9u7iKcC+RELGxknD3iIxwkiacd4Qdk\nTv6Jrl7vLLr6guG4uUIekc4osVfDeXkavSPczQLY6bWBqQEWpenG18zpMokZKhfs\nmQ/I+PHBk8UnAxNnzwRksfClWbUmIsAtJ+MZCGo39Gdbh8PfRTDt0BvbykJB/VpD\nk7D/SCvngPhcLiJgUb8XVUb0p+EhSR8lNbQkgYv52YUD3B0CcUspG/OnWsJogmvh\nAesjdYW0Co4AahmEUrGIaJaHRGCFyujSAYfkwtk9ccwHahtjwiqoZAwjrfU8cNen\niYY1RtvSO6VwsUrGK341XSdyrpMsZj+JGxuMDB7RelNd3yjP6E7eI/QFiCrdG8cH\nnXlBjdX6EfHuPTgLahiaVhboJ7AAlJTVUsVy4+giLymEtkNiaUvckOFPCfXfjqLu\nOgba6zdgVZW9WG4MmIoAK9Glvk4cUyBUP6jAXMRWu6UBtPqtrNz2n4rl0J7TPA68\nOnpovJOtkFdW3D/Wytno\n=fWlu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T19:03:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_ad