"10166dc2d065cfbc807f1b22d8ef4e334d81811d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/10166dc2d065cfbc807f1b22d8ef4e334d81811d"}],"sha":"059928a006873b97262a969c2de36b6c0e474f34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/059928a006873b97262a969c2de36b6c0e474f34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/794579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patricklafrance","id":794579,"login":"patricklafrance","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDU3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patricklafrance","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/commits/10166dc2d065cfbc807f1b22d8ef4e334d81811d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T17:46:07Z","email":"patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Patrick Lafrance"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T17:46:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(firefly): add createDeferredRegistrationsRunner test utility (#662)\n\n* feat(firefly): add createDeferredRegistrationsRunner test utility\n\nApplications testing a deferred registration update run had to hand-roll a\nharness reimplementing what ModuleManager and LocalModuleRegistry do, which\ndrifts from the real sequence.\n\nAdds a @squide/firefly/testing entry point exposing\ncreateDeferredRegistrationsRunner, a thin wrapper over the real module manager.\nAn update run is transactional and dispatches the update started and completed\nevents, matching what useUpdateDeferredRegistrations does at runtime. Modules\nlisten to those events to reset their per run state, so a runner omitting them\ndoesn''t reproduce a real application.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(firefly): cover the deferred registrations update event sequence\n\nA deferred registrations update run is a contract between two layers: the\nuseUpdateDeferredRegistrations hook dispatches the update events around the\nmodule manager, and modules react to those events to reset their per run state.\n\nNeither half was covered. Adds renderHook tests pinning the hook''s half, that\nthe started event is dispatched before the module manager update, the app router\nis notified in between, and the completed event is dispatched after even when\nthe run returns errors. Documents the other half, and why a runner cannot cover\nthe hook''s half since it stands in for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): reproduce the full update sequence in the registrations runner\n\nAn update run dispatches three event bus events, not two. Between the started\nand completed events, useEnhancedReducerDispatch updates the app router store\nand dispatches DeferredRegistrationsUpdatedEvent, which is publicly exported.\nThe runner omitted both, so a listener on that event never fired during a runner\ndriven update and deferredRegistrationsUpdatedAt was never advanced. The app\nrouter store is explicitly there for non-React consumers, so the documented\n\"doesn''t notify React\" caveat didn''t cover it.\n\nNarrows the runtime type parameter to FireflyRuntime, as the app router store is\na FireflyRuntime concept and the utility already imports firefly only events.\n\nAlso fixes two documentation examples calling update before register, which\nthrows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(smoke-test): stop the run from exhausting its turn budget\n\nThe smoke test aborted with \"Reached maximum number of turns (50)\" while\nevery page it reached rendered correctly. The same commit passed 9 minutes\nearlier using 48 of 50 turns, so the check has been a coin flip rather than\na signal.\n\nMost of the budget went to friction the prompt itself created:\n\n- `pnpm serve-endpoints > /tmp/... 2>&1 &` is unrunnable — the sandbox\n  blocks both `&` and file redirection — costing 2-3 turns every run.\n- `Bash(agent-browser:*)` does not match `node_modules/.bin/agent-browser`,\n  which the agent reaches for after `which`.\n- `agent-browser console` dumps 30-92 KB of `[log]`/`[warning]` lines, so it\n  spills to a file and needs an extra turn to read back, once per page.\n- LaunchDarkly errors fire on every page (`LAUNCH_DARKLY_CLIENT_ID` is never\n  set in CI) but were not listed as known noise, so each page needed triage.\n- Failure criteria included \"navigation links that lead nowhere\" while the\n  constraints allowed only `snapshot` and `console`. That contradiction sent\n  the passing run down a ~15-turn dead end trying to verify link clicks.\n\nThe prompt now states the shell constraints up front and gives one\ncopy-paste recipe per page that clears the console, navigates, waits,\nsnapshots and filters errors in a single turn. Raise `--max-turns` to 80 and\nallowlist the utilities the recipes pipe through instead of relying on\nundocumented default-allows.\n\nVerified against a local build of the endpoints sample: all six pages render\nreal content with no retries, the intentional 500 on the failing tab being\nthe only error. The recipe waits 8000ms because that tab''s error boundary\nhad not rendered at 5000ms, which is what forced a retry snapshot in both\nCI runs. New flow is ~13 turns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(smoke-test): revert workflow change, keep the prompt fix\n\n`claude-code-action@v1` refuses to run unless the calling workflow file is\nbyte-identical to the copy on `main`. Editing `smoke-test.yml` on this branch\nmade the action skip with \"Workflow validation failed\" — and the step still\nreported success, so the previous commit turned the smoke test into a green\ncheck that never launched the agent (4s step, no agent output).\n\nRestore `smoke-test.yml` to main''s content. The prompt rewrite is the part\nthat actually fixes the flake and it is read from the branch, so it takes\neffect here: the run drops from 48-51 turns to ~13, leaving ~4x headroom\nunder the existing 50-turn cap. The reverted `--max-turns 80` and the extra\n`Bash(grep|head|tail|echo:*)` entries were belt-and-braces — both prior runs\nalready used those utilities successfully without them being listed.\n\nDocument the validation rule in agent-docs/references/ci-cd.md so the next\nperson does not try to verify a change to these workflows on its own PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): reproduce the register run app router dispatches in the runner\n\nA register run also updates the app router store in a real application:\nmodules-registered and modules-ready are dispatched through\nuseEnhancedReducerDispatch, so after a registration areModulesRegistered and\nareModulesReady are true and deferredRegistrationsUpdatedAt is set. The runner\nleft all of them at their initial values, so a module or a widget library\nguarding on that state silently no-ops under a runner.\n\nDerives the headless wait state from the runtime rather than hardcoding it, as\nwaitForMsw is derived from the runtime and not from the AppRouter state, and\nbuilds it per dispatch so listeners can''t leak a mutation across tests.\n\nAlso documents that a runner needs a plugin wired runtime, since\ninitializeFirefly always registers an EnvironmentVariablesPlugin and cannot be\nused in tests, renames a hook test that promised more than it verified, and adds\ncoverage for the rejecting update path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(firefly): rename testing.test.tsx after the function under test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): make the runner update wait for an unawaited registration run\n\nThe registration guard was a boolean flipped before the run completed, so it\nonly guarded a second register call. A test forgetting the await on register\nthen calling update passed the guard and failed deep inside the module\nregistries with an unrelated message, after the started event had been\ndispatched. Keeping the promise makes the ordering deterministic.\n\nAlso replaces the _validateRegistrations documentation example. That function\nvalidates routes before navigation items, and routes registered without an\nexplicit parent default to the PublicRoutes and ProtectedRoutes outlets, which a\nheadless runner never registers, so it throws about a missing outlet for any\nmodule registering a route whatever the state of the navigation items.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): restore the runner registration promise guard\n\nThe previous commit landed the regression test without its fix, the source\nchange was reverted while restoring from a local mutation check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): serialize runner update runs and drop the unsatisfiable wait state\n\nDeriving waitForMsw from the runtime produced a wait state a runner can never\nsatisfy: the runner doesn''t run the MSW lifecycle, so isMswReady stays false and\na consumer combining the two concludes the application is bootstrapping forever.\nA headless run genuinely has nothing to wait for, so the flag is false like the\ntwo data ones.\n\nSerializes update runs against the previous run. Only the registration run was\nguarded, so two updates without an await opened a transactional registration\nscope while the previous one was still active.\n\nDerives the event name from the action type rather than passing both, as the\nconstants are a concatenation of \"squide-\" with the action type. Passing them\nindependently allowed a valid but mismatched pair to type check.\n\nAlso indexes the testing entry point in the agent specs README. The skill itself\nis synced from docs by the sync-agent-skill workflow on merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcbe4f22ad910d006558426b71bbf51f9f26a803","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/trees/dcbe4f22ad910d006558426b71bbf51f9f26a803"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/workleap/wl-squide/git/commits/10166dc2d065cfbc807f1b22d8ef4e334d81811d","verification":{"payload":"tree dcbe4f22ad910d006558426b71bbf51f9f26a803\nparent a309faf8500e0486a847f6c2bc453975b6bf88ad\nauthor Patrick Lafrance <patricklafrance@users.noreply.github.com> 1787593567 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787593567 -0400\n\nfeat(firefly): add createDeferredRegistrationsRunner test utility (#662)\n\n* feat(firefly): add createDeferredRegistrationsRunner test utility\n\nApplications testing a deferred registration update run had to hand-roll a\nharness reimplementing what ModuleManager and LocalModuleRegistry do, which\ndrifts from the real sequence.\n\nAdds a @squide/firefly/testing entry point exposing\ncreateDeferredRegistrationsRunner, a thin wrapper over the real module manager.\nAn update run is transactional and dispatches the update started and completed\nevents, matching what useUpdateDeferredRegistrations does at runtime. Modules\nlisten to those events to reset their per run state, so a runner omitting them\ndoesn''t reproduce a real application.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(firefly): cover the deferred registrations update event sequence\n\nA deferred registrations update run is a contract between two layers: the\nuseUpdateDeferredRegistrations hook dispatches the update events around the\nmodule manager, and modules react to those events to reset their per run state.\n\nNeither half was covered. Adds renderHook tests pinning the hook''s half, that\nthe started event is dispatched before the module manager update, the app router\nis notified in between, and the completed event is dispatched after even when\nthe run returns errors. Documents the other half, and why a runner cannot cover\nthe hook''s half since it stands in for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): reproduce the full update sequence in the registrations runner\n\nAn update run dispatches three event bus events, not two. Between the started\nand completed events, useEnhancedReducerDispatch updates the app router store\nand dispatches DeferredRegistrationsUpdatedEvent, which is publicly exported.\nThe runner omitted both, so a listener on that event never fired during a runner\ndriven update and deferredRegistrationsUpdatedAt was never advanced. The app\nrouter store is explicitly there for non-React consumers, so the documented\n\"doesn''t notify React\" caveat didn''t cover it.\n\nNarrows the runtime type parameter to FireflyRuntime, as the app router store is\na FireflyRuntime concept and the utility already imports firefly only events.\n\nAlso fixes two documentation examples calling update before register, which\nthrows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(smoke-test): stop the run from exhausting its turn budget\n\nThe smoke test aborted with \"Reached maximum number of turns (50)\" while\nevery page it reached rendered correctly. The same commit passed 9 minutes\nearlier using 48 of 50 turns, so the check has been a coin flip rather than\na signal.\n\nMost of the budget went to friction the prompt itself created:\n\n- `pnpm serve-endpoints > /tmp/... 2>&1 &` is unrunnable — the sandbox\n  blocks both `&` and file redirection — costing 2-3 turns every run.\n- `Bash(agent-browser:*)` does not match `node_modules/.bin/agent-browser`,\n  which the agent reaches for after `which`.\n- `agent-browser console` dumps 30-92 KB of `[log]`/`[warning]` lines, so it\n  spills to a file and needs an extra turn to read back, once per page.\n- LaunchDarkly errors fire on every page (`LAUNCH_DARKLY_CLIENT_ID` is never\n  set in CI) but were not listed as known noise, so each page needed triage.\n- Failure criteria included \"navigation links that lead nowhere\" while the\n  constraints allowed only `snapshot` and `console`. That contradiction sent\n  the passing run down a ~15-turn dead end trying to verify link clicks.\n\nThe prompt now states the shell constraints up front and gives one\ncopy-paste recipe per page that clears the console, navigates, waits,\nsnapshots and filters errors in a single turn. Raise `--max-turns` to 80 and\nallowlist the utilities the recipes pipe through instead of relying on\nundocumented default-allows.\n\nVerified against a local build of the endpoints sample: all six pages render\nreal content with no retries, the intentional 500 on the failing tab being\nthe only error. The recipe waits 8000ms because that tab''s error boundary\nhad not rendered at 5000ms, which is what forced a retry snapshot in both\nCI runs. New flow is ~13 turns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(smoke-test): revert workflow change, keep the prompt fix\n\n`claude-code-action@v1` refuses to run unless the calling workflow file is\nbyte-identical to the copy on `main`. Editing `smoke-test.yml` on this branch\nmade the action skip with \"Workflow validation failed\" — and the step still\nreported success, so the previous commit turned the smoke test into a green\ncheck that never launched the agent (4s step, no agent output).\n\nRestore `smoke-test.yml` to main''s content. The prompt rewrite is the part\nthat actually fixes the flake and it is read from the branch, so it takes\neffect here: the run drops from 48-51 turns to ~13, leaving ~4x headroom\nunder the existing 50-turn cap. The reverted `--max-turns 80` and the extra\n`Bash(grep|head|tail|echo:*)` entries were belt-and-braces — both prior runs\nalready used those utilities successfully without them being listed.\n\nDocument the validation rule in agent-docs/references/ci-cd.md so the next\nperson does not try to verify a change to these workflows on its own PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): reproduce the register run app router dispatches in the runner\n\nA register run also updates the app router store in a real application:\nmodules-registered and modules-ready are dispatched through\nuseEnhancedReducerDispatch, so after a registration areModulesRegistered and\nareModulesReady are true and deferredRegistrationsUpdatedAt is set. The runner\nleft all of them at their initial values, so a module or a widget library\nguarding on that state silently no-ops under a runner.\n\nDerives the headless wait state from the runtime rather than hardcoding it, as\nwaitForMsw is derived from the runtime and not from the AppRouter state, and\nbuilds it per dispatch so listeners can''t leak a mutation across tests.\n\nAlso documents that a runner needs a plugin wired runtime, since\ninitializeFirefly always registers an EnvironmentVariablesPlugin and cannot be\nused in tests, renames a hook test that promised more than it verified, and adds\ncoverage for the rejecting update path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(firefly): rename testing.test.tsx after the function under test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): make the runner update wait for an unawaited registration run\n\nThe registration guard was a boolean flipped before the run completed, so it\nonly guarded a second register call. A test forgetting the await on register\nthen calling update passed the guard and failed deep inside the module\nregistries with an unrelated message, after the started event had been\ndispatched. Keeping the promise makes the ordering deterministic.\n\nAlso replaces the _validateRegistrations documentation example. That function\nvalidates routes before navigation items, and routes registered without an\nexplicit parent default to the PublicRoutes and ProtectedRoutes outlets, which a\nheadless runner never registers, so it throws about a missing outlet for any\nmodule registering a route whatever the state of the navigation items.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): restore the runner registration promise guard\n\nThe previous commit landed the regression test without its fix, the source\nchange was reverted while restoring from a local mutation check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(firefly): serialize runner update runs and drop the unsatisfiable wait state\n\nDeriving waitForMsw from the runtime produced a wait state a runner can never\nsatisfy: the runner doesn''t run the MSW lifecycle, so isMswReady stays false and\na consumer combining the two concludes the application is bootstrapping forever.\nA headless run genuinely has nothing to wait for, so the flag is false like the\ntwo data ones.\n\nSerializes update runs against the previous run. Only the registration run was\nguarded, so two updates without an await opened a transactional registration\nscope while the previous one was still active.\n\nDerives the event name from the action type rather than passing both, as the\nconstants are a concatenation of \"squide-\" with the action type. Passing them\nindependently allowed a valid but mismatched pair to type check.\n\nAlso indexes the testing entry point in the agent specs README. The skill itself\nis synced from docs by the sync-agent-skill workflow on merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjINfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA2QQADcqq9cq8Wv+tE21PxgRz6Qm\nOGcbeJEOwuzWtOXuePGk77xW+0Ooh8A2apR2LnPSJt/g2AdsVgHbOEcBA2g/CKnv\nSPB8kbXIFKK21SmTNSA0mzYgKt0ETGjmbBNJd7EOEFd4q0DbdY4ctDjElPi47lXY\nM+rlLlS7LXdAnTx0uMVkFpM7Z7sPGq6DLZFo841D4Dd5R9S1pW06v1WcF5t5tcFG\nPr7DocyVG1EdZKbR7H04Ag4o4kKqURQgPts+IyC7lb5ZwBDBRk0ye2Z+RITIgad3\nIoTZaoJRc88nHx4jG633kLLonzAhsTFj3OkIvr6NvCJOwf9CYK3GUY9zypHSrd/W\nZIavy6vkMWs7gQ2zcMamNOlXVPk4PuLfDSS+hlYAuhxmDKapBdeJcOTJADASY8wR\n5jjU+lVuItKe6ePf5seqV+UprC0bPDfwblH3RZ47OfGZtWcPUaGvw+JlRVwuaOz7\nqp+fVQk9wCHR2USgsqfEbvXEqhJODql4fR4rl1BvaC/MxAp/GMw3S5lQq8UhuhTO\n/O0edIBOQMFQNjtKBoah2tvywRvUBKH7r9N2x4KCus1R1HaFsGm4u7b3Pc2Ofh4V\nXS7t8RksTnnHgz+/hCD3i8IP3/asvuDGQ9Pbf4datMM3tDDq1Vb1v6B2Lqtlap/E\n69PbbCFhsAzQEYnaPCVM\n=wPl8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T17:46:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https: